\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The Spanish stock market falls 0.63% awaiting Eurozone and U.S. PMIs\b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Ibex\uc2  35 started Friday's session with a fall of 0.64%, which led the Madrid selective index to stand at 9,304.3 points, on a day marked by the publication of macro data such as GDP in Spain and retail sales in the United Kingdom.\par \par \uc2 Specifically, after closing yesterday with a decline of 0.76%, the Madrid trading floor struggled to maintain the 9,300-point level, following the news that Spain's GDP recovered its pre-pandemic level in the first quarter after growing by 0.6% up to March compared to the previous quarter and by 4.2% in year-on-year terms.\par \par \uc2 The markets will also be attentive to the publication of PMIs in France, Germany, the \b \highlight22\uc2 United Kingdom\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the eurozone, as well as to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the member of the Executive Board of the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 ECB\uc2 ), \uc2 Fabio Panetta\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the early stages of this Friday's session, the biggest rises in the \uc2 Ibex\uc2  35 were recorded by \uc2 Cellnex\uc2  (+0.22%) and Enag\u225\'00\'E1s (+0.22%), while on the other side, with the biggest falls, were \uc2 Grifols\uc2  (-2.35%), \uc2 Aena\uc2  (-2.1%), Colonial (-1.17%), Fluidra (-1.09%) and \uc2 Acciona\uc2 , whose shares fell by 1%.\par \par \uc2 The main European stock exchanges also opened the day with a negative sign: 0.86% for Frankfurt, 0.54% for Milan, 0.51% for Paris and 0.30% for London.\par \par \uc2 In the commodities market, the price of a barrel of Brent crude oil, the reference for the Old Continent, was at 73.60 dollars, with a decrease of 0.73%, while Texas crude was trading at 68.92 dollars, with a decrease of 0.85%.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the euro against the dollar was at 1.0921 'greenbacks', while the Spanish risk premium was around 89.6 points, with the interest rate demanded for the Spanish ten-year bond at 3.417%.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230623ej6n004yi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw109\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1635\pichgoal600
