dited), respectively, and recorded amortization expense of $2.6 million, $3.9 million, $5.1 million, $1.1 million, and $1.5 million during the years ended December 31, 2020, 2021 and 2022 and the three months ended March 31, 2022 and 2023 (unaudited), respectively. The carrying value of capitalized internal-use software was $6.8 million, $11.3 million and $12.7 million as of December 31, 2021 and 2022 and March 31, 2023 (unaudited), respectively.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Accrued liabilities\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Accrued liabilities consisted of the following (in thousands):\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 31,                                March 31, \par 2021                                        2022     2023 \par (unaudited) \par Physical damage claims payable              $        24,113   $         41,118   $   45,306 \par Accrued legal                               13,148   5,600    5,571 \par Indirect tax liabilities                    12,970   24,810   30,113 \par Income tax liabilities                      1,035    3,669    2,980 \par Trip-related accruals                       12,540   14,550   17,691 \par Accrued marketing                           6,639    9,795    6,934 \par Accrued compensation and employee benefits  5,011    9,013    8,530 \par Insurance-related accruals                  1,340    1,426    2,111 \par Other                                       7,134    15,383   13,404 \par $                                           83,930   $        125,364   $        132,640 \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 4.Leases\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company has entered into various noncancelable operating leases for its office space facilities with contractual lease periods expiring between 2023 and 2028. Certain of these arrangements contain escalating rent payment provisions, free rent, and tenant improvement allowances. Lease expense is recognized on a straight-line basis over the non-cancelable lease term.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-21\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The components of lease costs consisted of the following (in thousands):\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Year ended December 31,   Three months ended March 31, \par 2022                      2022    2023 \par (unaudited) \par Operating lease cost      $       5,598   $   1,293   $   1,532 \par Sublease income           (849)   (209)   (215) \par Total lease costs         $       4,749   $   1,084   $   1,317 \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lease terms and discount rates for operating leases were as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 31,                                      March 31, \par 2022                                              2022   2023 \par (unaudited) \par Weighted-average remaining lease term (in years)  4.24   4.90   4.03 \par Weighted-average discount rate                    6.75   %      7.00   %   6.75   % \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Supplemental cash flow information related to leases consisted of the following (in thousands):\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Year ended December 31,                                              Three months ended March 31, \par 2022                                                                 2022   2023 \par (unaudited) \par Cash paid for operating lease liabilities                            $      5,154   $   1,138   $   1,574 \par Right-of-use assets obtained in exchange for new leases liabilities  $      4,739   $   1,600   $   - \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of December 31, 2022, the future minimum lease payments required under operating leases were as follows (in thousands):\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2023                                 $   6,528 \par 2024                                 6,220 \par 2025                                 6,241 \par 2026                                 6,390 \par 2027                                 1,999 \par Thereafter                           106 \par Total lease payments                 27,484 \par Less: Imputed Interest               (4,196) \par Present value of lease liabilities   $ 