alue is calculated as the difference between the exercise price of the underlying stock option award and the estimated fair value of the Company's common stock. The total intrinsic values of options exercised during the years ended December 31, 2020, 2021 and 2022 and three months ended March 31, 2022 and 2023 (unaudited) were $2.7 million, $18.1 million, $10.7 million, $4.6 million, and $1.3 million, respectively.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The weighted average grant-date fair value per share of options granted during the years ended December 31, 2020, 2021 and 2022 and three months ended March 31, 2022 (unaudited) was $1.06, $5.72, $6.33, and $6.33, respectively. There were no options granted during the three months ended March 31, 2023 (unaudited). The fair value of options vested during the years ended December 31, 2020, 2021 and 2022 and three months ended March 31, 2022 and 2023 (unaudited) was $7.0 million, $9.8 million, $23.9 million, $7.5 million, and $4.6 million. respectively. The fair value is being expensed over the vesting period of the options, on a straight-line basis as the services are being provided.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-36\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A summary of restricted stock units is as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Number ofshares                                  Weightedaverage grantdate fair value \par Unvested units as of December 31, 2021           247,000     $   14.84 \par Granted                                          8,523,672   9.98 \par Canceled                                         (369,558)   10.32 \par Unvested units as of December 31, 2022           8,401,114   10.11 \par Granted                                          1,041,516   8.74 \par Canceled                                         (172,316)   9.24 \par Unvested units as of March 31, 2023 (unaudited)  9,270,314   $   9.96 \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In September 2021, the Company began granting RSUs that vest upon the satisfaction of both a service-based and a liquid