\par\par \b \uc2 Science Group PLC\uc2  Recommended Cash Aquisition of \uc2 TP Group plc\b0\par\par\uc2 16,160 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2022\par 08:00\par \uc2 Regulatory News Service\par \uc2 RNS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2022 \par \par \uc2 TIDMSAG TIDMTPG\par \par \uc2 RNS Number : 5790E\par \par \uc2 Science Group PLC\par \par \uc2 31 October 2022\par \par \uc2 31 October 2022\par \par \uc2 NOT FOR RELEASE, PUBLICATION OR DISTRIBUTION IN WHOLE OR IN PART, DIRECTLY OR INDIRECTLY, IN, INTO OR FROM ANY JURISDICTION WHERE TO DO SO WOULD CONSTITUTE A VIOLATION OF THE RELEVANT LAWS OF SUCH JURISDICTION\par \par \uc2 THIS ANNOUNCEMENT CONTAINS INSIDE INFORMATION\par \par \uc2 FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\par \par \uc2 RECOMMENDED CASH ACQUISITION\par \par \uc2 of\par \par \uc2 TP Group plc\par \par \uc2 ("\uc2 TP Group\uc2 " or the "Company")\par \par \uc2 by\par \par \uc2 Science Group plc\par \par \uc2 ("\uc2 Science Group\uc2 ")\par \par \uc2 to be effected by way of scheme of arrangement\par \par \uc2 under Part 26 of the Companies Act 2006\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 -- The independent boards of \uc2 Science Group\uc2  and \uc2 TP Group\uc2  are pleased to announce that they have reached agreement on the terms of a recommended cash acquisition pursuant to which \uc2 Science Group\uc2  shall acquire the entire issued and to be issued ordinary share capital of \uc2 TP Group\uc2  (not already owned by \uc2 Science Group\uc2 ). The Acquisition is to be effected by means of a Court--sanctioned scheme of arrangement under Part 26 of the Companies Act. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --      Under the terms of the Acquisition, \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders will be entitled to receive: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2.25 pence in cash per Share\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The Acquisition Price of 2.25 pence per Share represents a premium of approximately 190 per cent. to the Closing Price per Share of 0.78 pence on 28 October 2022 (being the latest practicable date prior to the date of this announcement).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The Acquisition values \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's entire issued, and to be issued, ordinary share capital at an equity value of approximately GBP17.53 million.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  has received a letter of intent from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hargreave Hale Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2 , for and on behalf of IFSL Marlborough UK Micro-Cap Growth Fund and IFSL Marlborough Nano-Cap Growth Fund (Canaccord Genuity Wealth Management) to vote in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the resolutions to be proposed at the General Meeting, in respect of a total of 91,180,000 Shares, representing approximately 11.70 per cent. of the ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  in issue on 28 October 2022 (being the latest practicable date prior to this announcement).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This summary should be read in conjunction with the full text of this announcement and its Appendices. The Acquisition will be subject to the Conditions and further terms set out in Appendix I to this announcement and to the full terms and conditions which will be set out in the Scheme Document. Appendix II to this announcement contains the sources of information and bases of calculations of certain information contained in this announcement. Appendix III contains a summary of the irrevocable undertakings received in relation to this Acquisition and Appendix IV contains definitions of certain expressions used in this summary and in this announcement. The appendices form part of this announcement. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Enquiries: \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par  Sarah Cole, Group Legal Counsel & Company        Tel: +44 (0) 1223 \par   Secretary                                        875 200 \par   \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jon Brett\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Group Finance Director \par  Stifel Nicolaus Europe Limited, exclusive \par   financial adviser, nominated adviser and \par   joint broker to Science Group \par  Nick Adams, Alex Price, Richard Short            Tel: +44 (0) 207710 \par                                                    7600 \par  \par  Liberum Capital Limited, Joint Broker \par   to Science Group \par  Neil Patel, Cameron Duncan                       Tel: +44 (0) 20 3100 \par                                                    2000 \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group plc\f28 \uc2 \f2                                      Tel: +44 (0) 1753 \par                                                    285802 \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Derren Stroud\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Chief Financial Officer \par   and Company Secretary \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cenkos Securities plc\f28 \uc2 \f2 , financial adviser,        Tel: +44 (0) 20 7397 \par   nominated adviser and broker to \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2          8980 \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Stephen Keys\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mark Connelly\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Callum Davidson \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 DLA Piper\f28 \uc2 \f2  UK LLP is retained as the legal adviser to Science \par   Group. CMS Cameron McKenna Nabarro Olswang LLP is retained \par   as the legal adviser to \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par  The person responsible for this announcement on behalf of \par   \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  is Sarah Cole, Group Legal Counsel and Company \par   Secretary. The person responsible for this announcement on \par   behalf of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  is \f28 \uc2 \f2 Derren Stroud\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Chief Financial Officer \par   and Company Secretary. \par        NOT FOR RELEASE, PUBLICATION OR DISTRIBUTION IN WHOLE OR \par    IN PART, DIRECTLY OR INDIRECTLY, IN, INTO OR FROM ANY JURISDICTION \par       WHERE TO DO SO WOULD CONSTITUTE A VIOLATION OF THE RELEVANT \par                        LAWS OF SUCH JURISDICTION \par              THIS ANNOUNCEMENT CONTAINS INSIDE INFORMATION \par                          FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE \par                             31 October 2022 \par                       RECOMMENDED CASH ACQUISITION \par                                    of \par                               \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                      ("\f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 " or the "Company") \par                                    by \par                            \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                            ("\f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 ") \par              to be effected by way of scheme of arrangement \par                 under Part 26 of the Companies Act 2006 \par  \par    1          Introduction \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The independent boards of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  are pleased to announce that they have reached agreement on the terms of a recommended cash acquisition pursuant to which \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  shall acquire the entire issued and to be issued ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  (not already owned by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 ). The Acquisition is to be effected by means of a Court--sanctioned scheme of arrangement under Part 26 of the Companies Act. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    2          The Acquisition \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2.1 Under the terms of the Acquisition, which will be subject to the Conditions and further terms set out below and in Appendix I to this announcement, and to be set out in the Scheme Document, \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders will be entitled to receive:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2.25 pence in cash per Share\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2.2 The Acquisition Price of 2.25 pence per \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share represents a premium of approximately 190 per cent. to the Closing Price per Share of 0.78 pence on 28 October 2022 (being the latest practicable date prior to the date of this announcement).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2.3 The Acquisition values \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's entire issued, and to be issued, ordinary share capital at an equity value of approximately GBP17.53 million.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2.4 If any dividend or other distribution or return of value is proposed, declared, made, paid or becomes payable by \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  in respect of the Shares on or after the date of this announcement and prior to the Effective Date, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  will have the right to reduce the value of the consideration payable for each Share by up to the amount per Share of such dividend, distribution or return of value. If any such dividend, distribution or return of value is paid or made after the date of this announcement and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  exercises its rights described above, any reference in this announcement to the consideration payable under the Acquisition shall be deemed to be a reference to the consideration as so reduced. Any exercise by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  of its rights referred to in this paragraph shall be subject to the Takeover Code and the Panel's consent and the subject of an announcement and, for the avoidance of doubt, shall not be regarded as constituting any revision or variation of the terms of the Acquisition.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2.5 Further details about the Acquisition (including the expected timetable and notices of the Court Meeting and the General Meeting) will be contained in the Scheme Document that will be distributed to \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders (along with the Forms of Proxy for use in connection with the Court Meeting and the General Meeting) as soon as practicable and, in any event, within 28 days of this announcement (unless otherwise agreed by the Panel). \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    3          Background to and reasons for the Acquisition and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's strategic plans \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.1 On 9 August 2021, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  acquired 79,308,596 Shares equivalent to approximately 10.2 per cent. of the voting shares in \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  at a price of 5.0 pence per share. The shares were acquired in the open market. This followed a period during which \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  had repeatedly sought to engage with the then board of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  with regard to exploring a strategic investment and/or a potential combination of the two companies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.2 A period of discussion then took place between \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , during which \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  requisitioned a general meeting of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders seeking changes to the board of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which culminated in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  formally withdrawing its possible offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  on 3 September 2021. At that point, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  held 188,049,663 Shares, equivalent to approximately 24.1 per cent. of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's issued voting share capital, making \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  the largest shareholder in \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The requisitioned meeting was held on 1 October 2021 and the resolutions to appoint \f28 \uc2 \f2 Martyn Ratcliffe\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Peter Bertram\f28 \uc2 \f2  as directors of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  were passed. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  currently holds 217,923,105 Shares representing 27.97 per cent. of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's voting shares.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.3 Since that time, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  has been actively managing its investment with two directors on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  board, including the Chair. Following these appointments, on 16 December 2021 Science Group provided \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  with an unsecured standby revolving credit facility for up to GBP5 million which is available until 30 September 2023. As of 28 October 2022, GBP1 million had been drawn down. Following the Acquisition, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  intends to withdraw the facility and assume the debt of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which together with an outstanding facility with \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , amounts to approximately GBP7 million. As announced by \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the restructuring of the business has been progressing with disposals of non-core business activities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Science Group PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Recommended Cash Aquisition of -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.4 Within the core \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , TPG Services continues to perform satisfactorily but TPG Maritime has been impacted by onerous legacy contracts which have resulted in substantial provisions having had to be taken (including prior year adjustments) and contracts now being renegotiated. Following changes within the TPG Maritime management, including the secondment of a senior manager from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  to lead the business, \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  has this morning further updated shareholders on the progress in the renegotiation of those contracts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.5 The Independent Science Group Directors consider that there are significant potential synergies with \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and that a combination would be attractive to the employees and customers of both organisations. \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  operates primarily in the Defence and Aerospace sectors which would be complementary to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's activities, with minimal overlap.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Employees and management\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.6 Science Group attaches great importance to the skills, experience and continued commitment of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's management and employees and believes that they will benefit from greater opportunities as a result of the Acquisition. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors intend to support the development of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  business through organic initiatives and by acquisitions and, as such, do not expect any material change to the core \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the business as a result of the Acquisition. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  will continue to support \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's management in the continuous review of the TPG Group's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ensure efficiency in the ordinary course of business.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.7 Science Group has not entered into, and has not had any discussions with respect to proposals to enter into, any form of incentivisation or any other arrangements with members of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's management.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.8 Prior to \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's annual general meeting on 28 June 2022, \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  did not have an active employee share option plan. Shareholders approved the adoption of a Performance Share Plan at the AGM and \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  had anticipated granting share options to key managers and employees in the near future.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.9 If the Acquisition proceeds, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  intends to grant share options to key managers and employees at \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  under \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's PSP Scheme. No grants will be made to any current \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors. These one-off grants would total in aggregate not more than 400,000 options. A resolution will be put to shareholders of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  at its next annual general meeting to propose that these one-off grants be incremental to the plan limit defined in the Performance Share Plan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.10 \f28 \uc2 \f2 David Lindsay\f28 \uc2 \f2  (Non-Executive Director) has confirmed that he will resign from the board of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  conditional upon, and with effect from, the Scheme becoming effective. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  anticipates that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Derren Stroud\f28 \uc2 \f2  (Chief Financial Officer) would remain in his role at \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  until the middle of 2023 to effect a smooth transition into SG Group and to complete the TPG Group's statutory audits.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.11 Save as described above, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not intend to make any material reduction to the headcount, or any material change to the conditions of employment or to the balance of skills and functions, of the employees or management of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's core businesses. \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  is currently seeking to dispose of its non-core Westek business. If that sale does not proceed, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  will review the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and location of that business.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Existing rights and pension schemes\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.12 The TPG Group makes contributions to various defined contribution pension schemes on behalf of a number of qualifying employees and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  intends that these arrangements would remain in place. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    3.13      No member of the TPG Group participates in a defined benefit pension scheme. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.14 Following completion of the Acquisition, the existing employment rights of the management and employees of the TPG Group will be fully safeguarded. Furthermore, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not intend to make any material changes to the terms and conditions of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's pension schemes, including the employer contributions, accrual of benefits for existing members or the rights of admission of new members.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Locations and headquarters\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.15 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  has no plans to change the locations where people presently work in core \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  businesses, including offices in Bristol, Portsmouth and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wincanton\f28 \uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's headquarters). \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  is currently seeking to dispose of its non-core Westek business. If that sale does not proceed, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  will review the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and location of that business.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.16 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not intend to redeploy the fixed assets of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's core businesses comprise a services business and a product business. Research and development is not relevant to the services business. The product business (Maritime) does not currently have a research and development function but \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  intends to make investment into this area related to TPG Maritime following the completion of the Acquisition, in the region of between 2 per cent. and 5 per cent. of TPG Maritime's annual revenue.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Trading Facilities\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.17 \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  is currently admitted to trading on AIM and, as set out in paragraph 13 below, prior to the Scheme becoming effective, a request will be made to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  to cancel trading in \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares on AIM, following which it is intended that \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  would be re-registered as a private limited company.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3.18 No statements in this paragraph 3 are "post-offer undertakings" for the purposes of Rule 19.5 of the Takeover Code. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    4          Recommendation \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 4.1 As certain of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Directors, namely \f28 \uc2 \f2 Martyn Ratcliffe\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Peter Bertram\f28 \uc2 \f2 , are also directors of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the board of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  has constituted a committee composed of the Independent \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors for the purposes of evaluating and recommending the Acquisition to Shareholders. The Non-Independent \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors have not participated in the appraisal of the Acquisition or the decision of the Independent \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors to recommend the Acquisition to Shareholders.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 4.2 The Independent \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, who have been so advised by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cenkos Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  on the financial terms of the Acquisition, consider the terms of the Acquisition to be fair and reasonable. In providing their advice to the Independent \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cenkos Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  has taken into account the commercial assessments of the Independent \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cenkos Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  is providing independent financial advice to the Independent \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors for the purposes of Rule 3 of the Takeover Code.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 4.3 Accordingly, the Independent \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors intend to recommend unanimously that \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders vote in favour or procure votes in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the resolutions to be proposed at the General Meeting (or, if \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  exercises its right to implement the Acquisition by way of a Takeover Offer, to accept such offer), as the Independent \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors have irrevocably undertaken to do so in respect of their own Shares, being a total of 3,253,847 Shares, representing, in aggregate, approximately 0.42 per cent. of the ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  in issue on 28 October 2022 (being the latest practicable date prior to this announcement). \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    5          Background to and reasons for the recommendation \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5.1 \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's share price has generally been weak since its admission to AIM in 2001. Having floated at 105 pence, the share price fell to 14 pence approximately 15 months later in October 2002. Over the following years, the share price subsequently rose to 95 pence in June 2008. Following the financial crisis the share price fell again sharply to a low of 11.5 pence in February 2009 and whilst it recovered to a peak of 59.50 pence during that year, the share price has generally trended downwards since then to its recent all-time low of 0.60 pence.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5.2 This trend in the share price highlights the continual challenges which have faced \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  over the past few years, impacted more recently by well-publicised onerous contracts. As previously announced, whilst TPG Services has experienced a relatively steady performance and is delivering revenue growth year-on-year with modest profitability, TPG Maritime's performance has suffered as a result of onerous legacy contracts entered into historically and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  board has focused its efforts on re-negotiating these contracts on improved terms. \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's financial performance has also been impacted by significant exceptional costs in respect of its M&A activity including the disposals of TPG Engineering Limited, Northstar and Sapienza. \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported an increase in adjusted operating loss from a profit of GBP0.9 million in the financial year 2020 to a loss of GBP1.6 million in the financial year 2021. On a non-adjusted basis, operating loss widened to GBP7.5 million in the financial year 2021 (financial year 2020 reported a GBP3.3 million loss).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5.3 \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  was pleased to announce that revised terms had been agreed in relation to a number of the onerous contracts including a significant UK contract. Despite this the Independent \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors recognise the ongoing challenges inherent within the business and the broader market conditions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5.4 The Independent \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors acknowledge the indicative proposal made by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  in 2021 to acquire \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's shares at a price of 6.5p. Since that time, as a result of continuing economic and political uncertainty, the wider AIM market has suffered significant losses with the AIM-All Share Index having fallen by approximately 36 per cent. Furthermore, as a result of the trading challenges highlighted above, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's board's expectations in terms of performance have been significantly reduced and the net debt position of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  has increased. In addition, the availability of further funding to \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  has reduced.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Science Group PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Recommended Cash Aquisition of -3-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5.5 The Independent \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, having received a proposal from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  to acquire the entire issued and to be issued share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  (not already owned by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) at 2.25 pence per Share in cash, consider that the substantial premium of approximately 190 per cent. to the current market price, represents an acceptable valuation for \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and provides certainty of a cash exit to \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders in volatile and challenging market conditions. As such, the Independent \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors recommend the Acquisition, believing it to be in the best interests of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders as a whole. In coming to this conclusion, the Independent \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors took the following factors into consideration:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the offer price represents an opportunity for \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders to realise their investment in \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  for cash at value equating to approximately 190 per cent. premium to its current market price;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- this share price premium is significantly higher than recent average bid premia multiples paid for other UK public companies over the same period; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the certainty of the cash offer should be weighed against the inherent uncertainty of the delivery of the future value that exists in the business, including general uncertain economic and market conditions, the remaining onerous contracts within the \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  business, ongoing supply chain issues, inflationary pressures and funding challenges. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    6          Letter of intent \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 6.1 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  has received a letter of intent from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hargreave Hale Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2 , for and on behalf of IFSL Marlborough UK Micro-Cap Growth Fund and IFSL Marlborough Nano-Cap Growth Fund (Canaccord Genuity Wealth Management) to vote in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the resolutions to be proposed at the General Meeting, in respect of a total of 91,180,000 Shares, representing approximately 11.70 per cent. of the ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  in issue on 28 October 2022 (being the latest practicable date prior to this announcement).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 6.2 Further details of this letter of intent are set out in Appendix III to this announcement. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    7          Information on Science Group \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7.1 Science Group is an international science, technology and consulting organisation comprising three operating divisions: R&D Consultancy; Regulatory & Compliance; and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Frontier Smart Technologies\f28 \uc2 \f2 . With offices throughout Europe and North America, two UK-based dedicated R&D innovation centres and employees fluent in many languages \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  supports a global client base.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7.2 The R&D Consultancy division provides science-led advisory and product/technology development services. The division combines science and engineering capabilities with expertise in key vertical sectors, namely: Medical; Consumer; Food & Beverage; and Industrial, Chemicals & Energy. The R&D Consultancy Division combines leading science and engineering capabilities with market and commercial expertise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7.3 The Regulatory & Compliance division provides scientific and regulatory advice together with registration and compliance services for the Chemicals, Consumer, Food & Beverage and Medical sectors, which operate internationally in regulated markets. It includes the European and North American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of TSG and the Leatherhead Food Research business.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7.4 Frontier Smart Technologies is a market leading provider of DAB/DAB+/SmartRadio technology to the consumer electronics market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7.5 As described in more detail in paragraph 12 below, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  also has a strategic shareholding in \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  consisting of 217,923,105 Shares and representing 27.97 per cent. of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's issued voting share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  in issue as at 28 October 2022 (being the latest practicable date prior to this announcement).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7.6 The SG Group has a very strong balance sheet with significant cash resources and freehold property asset base, Harston Mill near Cambridge and Great Burgh in Epsom, together valued in the range of between GBP21 million to GBP35 million, as at the date of the last independent valuation in March 2021. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    8          Information on \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  is a specialist provider of technical consulting services and technologies to the defence and aerospace industries. \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  (previously called \f28 \uc2 \f2 Corac Group plc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) was admitted to trading on AIM in 2001, having initially been formed in 1996 to research and develop a number of traditional technologies within the field of compressed air. Since then, \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  has undergone several changes in strategic direction, with a view to maximising shareholder value through application of its technical capabilities within the engineering, industrial, defence and aerospace industries. Its business is currently focused on the UK defence and aerospace markets carried out through its two operating divisions - TPG Services and TPG Maritime. TPG Services provides technical expertise for the successful delivery of large, complex and critical programmes. TPG Maritime designs, manufactures, and supports life support systems for submarine programmes. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    9          \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share Schemes \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  has share options and warrants outstanding over, in aggregate, 25,192,028 Shares. The price that would be payable per Share to exercise these share options and warrants is higher than the Acquisition Price offered by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Therefore, no proposals under Rule 15 of the Takeover Code will be made to option-holders or warrant-holders and the share options and warrants will lapse, if unexercised, after the Scheme becomes effective. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    10        Financing \par    10.1      The Acquisition will be nanced from the existing cash resources of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10.2 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Stifel\f28 \uc2 \f2 , financial adviser to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , is satisfied that sufficient resources are available to satisfy in full the cash consideration payable to \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders under the terms of the Acquisition. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    11        Structure of and Conditions to the Acquisition \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11.1 The Acquisition will be effected by means of the Scheme, although \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  reserves the right to elect to implement the acquisition by means of a Takeover Offer (subject to Panel consent).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11.2 The purpose of the Scheme is to provide for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  to become the holder of the entire issued and to be issued ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  (not already owned by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 ). Following the Scheme becoming effective, the Scheme Shares will be transferred to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , in consideration for which Scheme Shareholders whose names appear on the register of members of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  at the Scheme Record Time will receive 2.25 pence per Scheme Share in cash.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11.3 Shares issued after the Scheme Record Time will not be subject to the Scheme. Accordingly, it is proposed that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Articles be amended so that Shares issued after the Scheme Record Time other than to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  will be automatically acquired by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  on the same terms as under the Scheme.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11.4 The Acquisition will be subject to the Conditions and further terms set out in Appendix I to this announcement and to be set out in the Scheme Document. The Acquisition is conditional upon the Scheme becoming unconditional and effective, subject to the Takeover Code, on or before 11:59 pm on the Long-Stop Date or such later date (if any) as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  may agree and the Panel and the Court may allow. In summary, the Scheme will be conditional, amongst other things, upon the following events occurring on or before 11:59 pm on the Long-Stop Date:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the approval of a majority in number of the Scheme Shareholders present and voting (and entitled to vote), either in person or by proxy, at the Court Meeting (or any adjournment thereof), representing not less than 75 per cent in value of the Scheme Shares held by such Scheme Shareholders;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the resolutions required to approve and implement the Scheme, as set out in the notice of the General Meeting, being duly passed by the requisite majorities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders at the General Meeting (or at any adjournment thereof);\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the sanction of the Scheme by the Court (without modification or with modification on terms acceptable to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) and the delivery of an office copy of the Court Order to the Registrar of Companies;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the satisfaction of the NSIA condition set out in paragraph 3.3 of the Conditions being satisfied or waived;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the satisfaction of the FATA condition set out in paragraph 3.4 of the Conditions being satisfied or waived; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the other conditions not otherwise identified above (but set out in Appendix I of this announcement) either being satisfied or, with the exception of certain conditions which are not capable of waiver, waived. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    11.5      The Scheme will lapse if: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the Court Meeting and the General Meeting are not held by the 22nd day after the expected date of such meetings to be set out in the Scheme Document in due course (or such later date as may be agreed between \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 );\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the Court Hearing is not held by the 22nd day after the expected date of such hearing to be set out in the Scheme Document in due course (or such later date as may be agreed between \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 ); or \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --      the Scheme does not become effective on or before 11:59 pm on the Long-stop Date, \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 provided, however, that the deadlines for the timing of the Court Meeting, the General Meeting and the Court Hearing as set out above may be waived by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , and the deadline for the Scheme to become effective may be extended by agreement between \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  with the consent of the Panel and, if required, the Court.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11.6 Subject to the satisfaction (or waiver, where applicable) of the Conditions, the Scheme is expected to become effective in the first quarter of 2023.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Science Group PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Recommended Cash Aquisition of -4-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11.7 Upon the Scheme becoming effective, it shall be binding on all \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders, irrespective of whether or not they attended or voted at the Court Meeting or the General Meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11.8 Further details of the Scheme, including an indicative timetable for its implementation, will be set out in the Scheme Document, which will be distributed to \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders as soon as practicable and, in any event, within 28 days of this announcement (unless otherwise agreed by the Panel, TP Group and Science Group). \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    12        Disclosure of interests in \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 12.1 As at the close of business on 28 October 2022, being the last Business Day prior to the date of this announcement, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and, so far as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  is aware, other persons acting, or deemed to be acting, in concert with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , held 217,923,105 Shares, representing 27.97 p er cent. of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's issued voting share capital as at 28 October 2022 (being the last practicable day prior to the date of this announcement) .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 12.2 As at the close of business on 28 October 2022, being the last practicable day prior to the date of this announcement, save as disclosed in paragraph 12.1 above and save for the irrevocable undertakings and the letter of intent referred to in Appendix III, none of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  or any \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors or, so far as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  is aware, any person acting, or deemed to be acting, in concert with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --      had an interest in, or right to subscribe for, relevant securities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  ; \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- had any short position in (whether conditional or absolute and whether in the money or otherwise), including any short position under a derivative, any agreement to sell or any delivery obligation or right to require another person to purchase or take delivery of, relevant securities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  ;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- had procured an irrevocable commitment or letter of intent to accept the terms of the Acquisition in respect of relevant securities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  ; or \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --      had borrowed or lent any Shares. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 12.3 Furthermore, save for the irrevocable undertakings and letter of intent described in Appendix III, no arrangement exists between \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  or \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  or a person acting in concert with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  or \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  in relation to Shares. For these purposes, an "arrangement" includes any indemnity or option arrangement, any agreement or any understanding, formal or informal, of whatever nature, relating to Shares which may be an inducement to deal or refrain from dealing in such securities. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    13        Cancellation of trading and re-registration \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 13.1 Prior to the Scheme becoming effective (or, if the Acquisition is effected by way of a Takeover Offer, on such Takeover Offer becoming or being declared wholly unconditional in all respects and sufficient acceptances having been received in respect of such offer), \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  will apply to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  for the cancellation of trading in the Shares on AIM to take effect on and from or shortly after the Effective Date. The last day of dealings in the Shares is expected to be the Business Day immediately prior to the Scheme becoming effective.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 13.2 On the Effective Date, share certificates in respect of Shares will cease to be valid and entitlements to Shares held within the CREST system will be cancelled or transferred. It is also proposed that, following the Effective Date, \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  will be re-registered as a private limited company. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    14        Overseas shareholders \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 14.1 The availability of the Acquisition or the distribution of this announcement to \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders who are not resident in the United Kingdom may be affected by the laws of their relevant jurisdiction. Such persons should inform themselves of, and observe, any applicable legal or regulatory requirements of their jurisdiction. \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders who are in any doubt regarding such matters should consult an appropriate independent professional adviser in the relevant jurisdiction without delay.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 14.2 This announcement does not constitute an offer for sale of any securities or an offer or an invitation to purchase any securities. \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders are advised to read carefully the Scheme Document and related Forms of Proxy once these have been published. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    15        General \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 15.1 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  reserves the right to elect, with the consent of the Panel, to implement the Acquisition by way of a Takeover Offer for the entire issued and to be issued ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  as an alternative to the Scheme. In such an event, the Takeover Offer will be implemented on the same terms or, if \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  so decides, on such other terms being no less favourable (subject to appropriate amendments), so far as applicable, as those which would apply to the Scheme and subject to the amendment referred to in Appendix I to this announcement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 15.2 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Stifel\f28 \uc2 \f2  (as financial adviser to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 ), \f28 \uc2 \f2 Liberum\f28 \uc2 \f2  (as joint broker to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cenkos Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  (as financial adviser to \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) have each given and not withdrawn their consent to the publication of this announcement with the inclusion herein of the references to their respective names and (where applicable) advice in the form and context in which they appear.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 15.3 The bases and sources of certain financial information contained in this announcement are set out in Appendix II to this announcement. A summary of the irrevocable undertakings and letter of intent received by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  is contained in Appendix III to this announcement. Certain terms used in this announcement are defined in Appendix IV to this announcement \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    16        Documents published on websites \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 16.1 Copies of this announcement, the irrevocable undertakings and the letter of intent referred to in Appendix III and the consents referred to in paragraphs 15.1 and 15.2 above, will be made available on \f28 \uc2 \f2 TP Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Science Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.tpglobalgroup.com/investors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.tpglobalgroup.com/investors}}}\uc2 \f2  and \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sciencegroup.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2