 against the dollar, while the British pound depreciated 1.6%, as investors remain cautious about possible imbalances in public finances.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the largest assets in the cryptocurrency market, advanced 0.25%, despite greater risk aversion.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the main stock indexes in the United States start the day with mixed movements. In Europe, there were generalized declines, with the Euro Stoxx decreasing 0.52%. Asia closed with losses, with the \uc2 Hang Seng\uc2  dropping 3.4% and the Shanghai 1.6%, following the cautious sentiment.\par \par \uc2 In Mexico, the Prices and Quotations Index could be consolidating around 44,800 points, according to estimates by Banorte specialists.\par \par \uc2 Finally, the price of US WTI oil opens with a gain of 1.31%, on speculation that OPEC+ could cut production despite signs of a possible accumulation of inventories in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Subscribe here to receive our newsletters about news of the day, opinion, weekend plans, Qatar 2022 and many more options.\par \par \uc2 vcr/mcc\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220929ei9s000jd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
