....                                    \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Adoption of IFRS 16 Leases\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fiscal year 2020 was the first fiscal year in which we have prepared our financial statements following adoption of IFRS 16 Leases. The application of IFRS 16 has resulted in a material gross up of the Consolidated Balance Sheet and a reclassification of charges previously booked to cost of sales and operating expenses to depreciation and interest expense. The impact on the Consolidated Statement of Comprehensive Income is not significant as included in the allocated cost of sales is the portion of depreciation and amortization expense attributable to the portion of our property and equipment and intangible assets utilized in the delivery of services to our clients, including depreciation of right-of-use assets. The net impact on profit before tax is immaterial and the approach to adopting the new standard has not required comparative information to be restated.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Comparison of the Years Ended June 30, 2021 and 2020\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Revenue\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                                                                       Year Ended June 30,           % Change\par                                                                                                       2021                            2020   2021 vs.\par                                                                                                                                       2020\par                                                                                                       (pounds in thousands)          \par Revenue................................................................................................\u163\'00\'A3 446,298 \u163\'00\'A3             350,950 27.2%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2021 Compared to 2020. Revenue for 2021 was \u163\'00\'A3446.3 million, an increase of \u163\'00\'A395.3 million, or 27.2%, over 2020. In constant \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  terms, revenue grew by 29.6% over 2020. We achieved significant growth in revenue across all verticals. Revenue from clients in the Payments and Financial Services vertical increased by \u163\'00\'A341.2 million, or 22.3%, to \u163\'00\'A3226.4 million in 2021 from \u163\'00\'A3185.2 million in 2020. Revenue from clients in the TMT vertical increased by \u163\'00\'A330.8 million, or 34.1%, to \u163\'00\'A3121.0 million in 2021 from \u163\'00\'A390.3 million in 2020. Revenue from clients in our Other vertical also grew significantly, increasing by \u163\'00\'A323.3 million, or 30.9%, to \u163\'00\'A398.9 million in 2021 from \u163\'00\'A375.5 million in 2020. The acquired \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of CDS contributed \u163\'00\'A327.2 million in 2021, particularly within our\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other vertical and in Europe. The acquired \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Five contributed \u163\'00\'A34.8 million in 2021, particularly within our Other and TMT verticals and in North America. The acquired \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Levvel contributed \u163\'00\'A311.6 million in 2021, particularly within our Other and Payments and Financial Services verticals and in North America. Revenue also grew across all geographies. Revenue from clients based in Europe increased by \u163\'00\'A322.1 million, or 25.7%, to \u163\'00\'A3108.0 million in 2021 from \u163\'00\'A385.9 million in 2020. Revenue from clients based in the United Kingdom increased by \u163\'00\'A331.5 million, or 20.3%, to \u163\'00\'A3187.0 million in 2021 from \u163\'00\'A3155.5 million in 2020. Revenue from clients based in North America increased by \u163\'00\'A340.0 million, or 40.0%, to \u163\'00\'A3140.1 million in 2021 from \u163\'00\'A3100.1 million in 2020. Revenue from clients based in Rest of World increased by \u163\'00\'A31.7 million, or 18.1%, to \u163\'00\'A311.2 million in 2021 from \u163\'00\'A39.5 million in 2020. Revenue from our top 10 clients in 2021 increased by \u163\'00\'A322.1 million, or 16.6%, to \u163\'00\'A3155.9 million compared to \u163\'00\'A3133.8 million in revenue from our top 10 clients in 2020.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cost of Sales\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                                                                       Year Ended June 30,     % Change\par                                                                                                       2021                              2020        2021 vs.\par                                                                                                                                         2020\par                                                                                                       (pounds in thousands)    \par Cost of sales                                                                                                                                        \par Direct cost of sales ..........................................................................     \u163\'00\'A3 (271,707)             \u163\'00\'A3 (233,352) 16.4%\par Allocated cost of sales.....................................................................          (20,758)                          (17,447)  19.0%\par .................................................................Total Cost of sales                \u163\'00\'A3 (292,465)               \u163\'00\'A3         (250,799)   16.6%\par Gross margin ........................................................................................  34.5%                             28.5%        \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2021 Compared to 2020. Total cost of sales increased by \u163\'00\'A341.7 million, or 16.6%, in 2021 compared to 2020. The increase consisted of a \u163\'00\'A338.4 million increase in direct cost of sales, as a result of increased personnel costs, which reflected an increase in the average number of employees involved in delivery of our services from 5,633 in 2020 to 6,943 in 2021. Our growth in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  headcount consisted of new employees located in Europe in connection with our acquisitions of CDS and Five and new employees in the Americas in connection with our acquisitions of Five and Levvel. Grant income decreased by \u163\'00\'A30.2 million in 2021 compared to 2020 and research and development credits (in respect of innovative work we carried out for contract customers) increased by \u163\'00\'A31.0 million in 2021 compared to 2020. Included in the allocated cost of sales is the portion of depreciation and amortization expense attributable to the portion of our property and equipment and intangible assets utilized in the delivery of services to our clients. This increased by \u163\'00\'A33.3 million in 2021 compared to 2020, or 19.0% due to the increase in size of our delivery organization. Gross margin increased to 34.5% in 2021 from 28.5% in 2020.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Selling, General and Administrative Expenses\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                              Year Ended June 30,              % Change\par                                              2021                             2020   2021 vs.\par                                                                    2020\par                                              (pounds in thousands)             \par Selling, general and administrative expenses \u163\'00\'A3 (90,290)            \u163\'00\'A3 (75,110) 20.2%\par % of revenue                                 (20.2)%               (21.4)%          \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2021 Compared to 2020. Selling, general and administrative expenses increased by \u163\'00\'A315.2 million, or 20.2%, in 2021 compared to 2020. The increase in