\par\par \b \uc2 SIMEC Atlantis Energy Limited\uc2  Placing announcement\b0\par\par\uc2 16,369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2021\par 18:22\par \uc2 Regulatory News Service\par \uc2 RNS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2021 \par \par \uc2 TIDMSAE\par \par \uc2 RNS Number : 2823N\par \par \uc2 SIMEC Atlantis Energy Limited\par \par \uc2 28 September 2021\par \par \uc2 RNS\par \par \uc2 THIS ANNOUNCEMENT CONTAINS INSIDE INFORMATION FOR THE PURPOSES OF THE MARKET ABUSE REGULATION (\uc2 EU\uc2 ) NO. 596/2014 AS IT FORMS PART OF DOMESTIC LAW OF THE UNITED KINGDOM BY VIRTUE OF THE \uc2 EUROPEAN UNION\uc2  (WITHDRAWAL) ACT 2018, AS AMENDED ("MAR"). IN ADDITION, MARKET SOUNDINGS (AS DEFINED IN MAR) WERE TAKEN IN RESPECT OF THE MATTERS CONTAINED IN THIS ANNOUNCEMENT, WITH THE RESULT THAT CERTAIN PERSONS BECAME AWARE OF INSIDE INFORMATION (AS DEFINED IN MAR), AS PERMITTED BY MAR. THIS INSIDE INFORMATION IS SET OUT IN THIS ANNOUNCEMENT. THEREFORE, THOSE PERSONS THAT RECEIVED INSIDE INFORMATION IN A MARKET SOUNDING ARE NO LONGER IN POSSESSION OF SUCH INSIDE INFORMATION RELATING TO THE COMPANY AND ITS SECURITIES.\par \par \uc2 THIS ANNOUNCEMENT, INCLUDING THE APPENDIX HERETO AND THE INFORMATION CONTAINED HEREIN, IS RESTRICTED AND IS NOT FOR PUBLICATION, DISTRIBUTION OR RELEASE, DIRECTLY OR INDIRECTLY, IN WHOLE OR IN PART, IN OR INTO OR FROM THE UNITED STATES (INCLUDING ITS TERRITORIES AND POSSESSIONS, ANY STATES OF THE UNITED STATES AND THE DISTRICT OF COLUMBIA) (COLLECTIVELY, THE "UNITED STATES"), CANADA, AUSTRALIA, JAPAN OR THE REPUBLIC OF SOUTH AFRICA OR IN OR INTO OR FROM ANY OTHER JURISDICTION IN WHICH SUCH PUBLICATION, DISTRIBUTION OR RELEASE WOULD BE PROHIBITED BY ANY APPLICABLE LAW.\par \par \uc2 THIS ANNOUNCEMENT IS FOR INFORMATION PURPOSES ONLY AND IS NOT AND DOES NOT CONSTITUTE, CONTAIN OR FORM PART OF AN OFFER TO SELL OR ISSUE OR A SOLICITATION TO BUY, SUBSCRIBE FOR OR OTHERWISE ACQUIRE, ANY SECURITIES IN THE UNITED STATES, CANADA, AUSTRALIA, JAPAN OR THE REPUBLIC OF SOUTH AFRICA OR ANY OTHER JURISDICTION IN WHICH ANY SUCH OFFER OR SOLICITATION WOULD BE UNLAWFUL.THIS ANNOUNCEMENT SHOULD BE READ IN ITS ENTIRETY.\par \par \uc2 IN PARTICULAR, YOU SHOULD READ AND UNDERSTAND THE INFORMATION PROVIDED IN THE APPENDIX WHICH CONTAINS THE TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF THE PLACING.\par \par \uc2 28 September 2021\par \par \uc2 SIMEC Atlantis Energy Limited\par \par \uc2 ("SAE", the "Company" and, together with its subsidiaries, the "Group")\par \par \uc2 Proposed Placing of approximately 100,000,000 new Ordinary Shares at 2.5 pence per share to raise approximately GBP2.5 million for the Company\par \par \uc2 and\par \par \uc2 Termination of share placement agreement\par \par \uc2 Highlights\par \par \uc2 -- Proposed Placing at 2.5 pence per Ordinary Share to raise gross proceeds (before expenses) of approximately GBP2.5 million.\par \par \uc2 -- Placing to be conducted by way of an accelerated bookbuild process by Arden in accordance with the terms and conditions set out in the Appendix to this announcement. The accelerated bookbuild will commence immediately following this announcement.\par \par \uc2 -- The Placing Price represents a discount of 48.4 per cent. to the mid-market closing price of 4.85 pence on 28 September 2021, being the last practicable trading day prior to release of this announcement.\par \par \uc2 -- The net proceeds of the Placing are proposed to be used to fund the Group's working capital and the delivery of its 'first-of-a-kind' and world leading projects.\par \par \uc2 -- As SAE continues to develop its key projects, it remains dependent upon external financing. SAE is continuing to seek funding which is needed in the near term to support continuing Group \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the development of key projects, and the Board is considering a range of funding options for the Group including the disposal of certain non-core assets within the Group. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --               A further announcement will be made on the closing of the Placing. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The Group has also today published its interim results for the six months ended 30 June 2021 in a separate announcement. A copy of the interim results will be available on the Company's website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.simecatlantis.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.simecatlantis.com}}}\uc2 \f2  . The interim results should be read in conjunction with this announcement and prospective investors should read the Group's interim results in full before making any bid in the Bookbuild. Attention is drawn to the Directors' assessment of going concern, described at Note 4 in the interim results.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition, SAE has today terminated the share placement agreement, announced in December 2020, with New Technology Capital Group, LLC. No further funds will be drawn down pursuant to the agreement. The balance of funds due to the subscriber of GBP930,000 will be settled as required through the issue of new SAE shares in due course, under the surviving terms of the facility.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Enquiries:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investec Bank plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  +44 (0) 20 7597 5970\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Nominated Adviser and Joint Broker to the Company)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jeremy Ellis\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ben Griffiths\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Arden Partners plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  +44 (0) 20 7614 5900\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Sole Bookrunner and Joint Broker to the Company)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ruari McGirr\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Richard Johnson\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Simon Johnson\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SIMEC Atlantis Energy Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  +44 (0) 7739 832 446\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sean Parsons, Director of External Affairs\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Notes to Editors\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SIMEC Atlantis Energy\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAE is a global developer, owner and operator of sustainable energy projects with a diverse portfolio in various stages of development. This includes a 77 per cent. stake in the world's largest tidal stream power project, MeyGen, 100 per cent. of the 220MW Uskmouth Power Station conversion project and 100 per cent. of Green Highland Renewables, a leading developer of mini-hydro projects.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.simecatlantis.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.simecatlantis.com/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 More on the MeyGen Project: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://simecatlantis.com/projects/meygen/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://simecatlantis.com/projects/meygen/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 More on the Uskmouth Project: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://simecatlantis.com/project-development-operation/simec-uskmouth-power/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://simecatlantis.com/project-development-\b  \highlight22operation\b0 \highlight22 /simec-uskmouth-power/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Market Abuse Regulation\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The information contained within this announcement is inside information as stipulated under MAR. Upon the publication of this announcement, this inside information is now considered to be in the public domain. The person responsible for arranging for the release of this announcement on behalf of \f28 \uc2 \f2 SIMEC Atlantis Energy\f28 \uc2 \f2  is \f28 \uc2 \f2 Graham Reid\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Chief Executive Officer of SIMEC Atlantis Energy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Important Notice\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This announcement does not constitute, or form part of, a prospectus relating to the Company, nor does it constitute or contain any invitation or offer to any person, or any public offer, to subscribe for, purchase or otherwise acquire any shares in the Company or advise persons to do so in any jurisdiction, nor shall it, or any part of it form the basis of or be relied on in connection with any contract or as an inducement to enter into any contract or commitment with the Company.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 T