s nor does it write options.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Sensitivity\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group is exposed to translation and transaction foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange risk. Several other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in addition to the presentation \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Sterling are used, including Romanian Lei (RON), Euro (EUR) and US Dollars (USD).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group experiences \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange differences arising upon retranslation of monetary items (primarily short-term inter-company balances and borrowings), which are recognised as an expense in the period the difference occurs. The Group endeavours to match the cash inflows and outflows in the various \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ; the Group typically invoices its clients in their local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and pays its local expenses in local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as a means to mitigate this risk.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  denominated financial assets and liabilities which expose the Group to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk are disclosed below. The amounts shown are translated into GBP at the closing rate:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 30, 2021         GBP\u163\'00\'A3'000 EUR\u163\'00\'A3'000 USD\u163\'00\'A3'000 RON\u163\'00\'A3'000 Others\u163\'00\'A3'000 TOTAL\u163\'00\'A3'000\par Financial assets      101,136  26,177   38,375   5,093    17,406      188,187\par Financial liabilities (41,448) (9,641)  (15,666) (53,533) (37,948)    (158,236)\par Total                 59,688   16,536   22,709   (48,440) (20,542)    29,951\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 30, 2020         GBP\u163\'00\'A3'000 EUR\u163\'00\'A3'000 USD\u163\'00\'A3'000 RON\u163\'00\'A3'000 Others\u163\'00\'A3'000 TOTAL \u163\'00\'A3'000\par Financial assets      133,613  14,802   21,060   5,324    9,142       183,941\par Financial liabilities (30,012) (7,703)  (5,885)  (37,733) (36,083)    (117,306)\par Total                 103,601  7,099    15,175   (32,409) (26,941)    66,635\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group is also exposed to exchange differences arising from the translation of its subsidiaries' financial statements into the Group's presentation \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Sterling with the corresponding exchange differences taken directly to equity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following tables illustrate the sensitivity of profit and equity in regards to the Group's financial assets and financial liabilities and the RON/Sterling exchange rate. The RON exposure impacts the majority of the Group's\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-67\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 cost base. Therefore as the Sterling strengthens, subject to any prevailing hedge arrangements, the Group benefits from a cost improvement and vice versa.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 During the year ended 30 June 2021 the Sterling/RON volatility ranged from the RON strengthening against Sterling by 5% to weakening by 5%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GBP/RON       Profit impact\u163\'00\'A3'000 Equity impact\u163\'00\'A3'000\par June 30, 2021 5                  % (820) (510)\par June 30, 2021 (5)                % 766   476\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 During the year ended 30 June 2020, the Sterling/RON volatility ranged from the RON strengthening against Sterling by 6% to weakening by 7%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GBP/RON       Profit impact\u163\'00\'A3'000 Equity impact\u163\'00\'A3'000\par June 30, 2020 6                  % (587) (522)\par June 30, 2020 (7)                % 722   641\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Interest Rate Sensitivity\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 30 June 2021, the Group is not exposed to changes in market interest rates through bank borrowings on its revolving credit facility at variable interest rates, as the facility is not drawn.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Credit Risk Analysis\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Credit risk is the risk that a counterparty fails to discharge an obligation to the Group. The Group is exposed to this risk for various financial instruments, including trade receivables. The Group's maximum exposure to credit risk is limited to the carrying amount of financial assets recognised at 30 June, as summarised below:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2021\u163\'00\'A3'00                    2020\u163\'00\'A3'000\par Cash and cash equivalents   \u163\'00\'A3       69,884  \u163\'00\'A3 101,327\par Trade and other receivables 118,303 82,614\par Total                       \u163\'00\'A3       188,187 \u163\'00\'A3 183,941\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group monitors defaults of clients and other counterparties, identified either individually, or by group, and incorporates this information into its credit risk controls. Where available at reasonable cost, external credit ratings and/or reports on clients and other counterparties are obtained and used.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Management considers that all financial assets that are not impaired or past due at the end of the applicable reporting period are of good credit quality. Some of the unimpaired trade receivables are generally past due as of the end of the applicable reporting period. Information on trade receivables past due but not impaired are as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2021\u163\'00\'A3'00                                      2020\u163\'00\'A3'000\par Not more than 3 months                        \u163\'00\'A3     10,671 \u163\'00\'A3 2,347\par More than 3 months but not more than 6 months 4,883 1,329\par More than 6 months but not more than 1 year   -     -\par More than 1 year                              -     -\par Total                                         \u163\'00\'A3     15,554 \u163\'00\'A3 3,676\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In respect of trade and other receivables, the Group is not exposed to any significant credit risk exposure to any single counterparty or any group of counterparties having similar characteristics.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-68\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group's trade receivables are from a large number of clients in various industries and geographical areas. Based on historical information about client default rates, management consider the credit quality of trade receivables that are not past due or impaired to be good.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The credit risk for cash and cash equivalents is considered negligible, since the counterparties are reputable banks with high quality external credit ratings.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Liquidity Risk Analysis\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group manages its liquidity needs by monitoring scheduled debt servicing payments for long-term financial liabilities as well as forecast cash inflows and outflows due in day-to-day business. The data used for analysing these cash flows is consistent with that used in the contractual maturity analysis below. Liquidity needs are monitored in various time bands, on a day-to-day and week-to-week basis, as well as on a longer-term basis. Net cash requirements are compared to available borrowing facilities in order to determine headroom or any shortfalls. This analysis shows that available borrowing facilities are expected to be sufficient over the lookout period.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group's objective is to maintain cash and marketable securities to meet its liquidity requirements for 30\u8209\'20\'11day periods at a minimum. This objective was met for all of the reporting periods presented.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group considers expected cash flows from financial assets in assessing and managing liquidity risk, in particular its cash resources and trade receivables. The Group's existing cash resources and trade receivables exceed the current cash outflow requirements. Cash flows from trade and other receivables are all contractually due within six months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As at 30 June 2021, the Group's non-derivative financial liabilities had contractual maturities (including interest payments where applicable) as summarised below:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Current0 - 6 months\u163\'00\'A3'000 Current6 - 12 months\u163\'00\'A3'000 Non-Current1 - 5 years\u163\'00\'A3'000 Non-Current+5 years\u163\'00\'A3'000\par Lease liabilities        \u163\'00\'A3                         7,173                       \u163\'00\'A3     6,324  \u163\'00\'A3 35,947 \u163\'00\'A3 14,241\par Trade and other payables 78,634                    -                           -     -\par Deferred consideration   624                       -                           9,370 -\par Contingent consideration -                         5,718                       -     -\par Other liabilities        -                         -                           205   -\par Total                    \u163\'00\'A3                         86,431                      \u163\'00\'A3     12,042 \u163\'00\'A3 45,522 \u163\'00\'A3 14,241\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There were no forward foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options in place at 30 June 2021.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As at 30 June 2020, the Group's non-derivative financial liabilities had contractual maturities (including interest payments where applicable) as summarised below:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Current0 - 6 months\u163\'00\'A3'000 Current6 - 12 months\u163\'00\'A3'000 Non-Current1 - 5 years\u163\'00\'A3'000 Non-Current+5 years\u163\'00\'A3'000\par Lease liabilities        \u163\'00\'A3                         5,652                       \u163\'00\'A3   5,480 \u163\'00\'A3 30,643 \u163\'00\'A3 11,590\par Trade and other payables 58,599                    -                           -   -\par Deferred consideration   1,970                     1,937                       -   -\par Contingent consideration -                         1,409                       -   -\par Other liabilities        -                         -                           136 -\par Total                    \u163\'00\'A3                         66,221                      \u163\'00\'A3   8,826 \u163\'00\'A3 30,779 \u163\'00\'A3 11,590\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-69\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 32.Capital Management Policies and Procedures\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group's capital management objectives are:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22to ensure the Group's ability to continue as a going concern; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22to provide an adequate return to shareholders by pricing products and services commensurately with the level of risk.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group monitors capital on the basis of the carrying amount of equity plus loan, less cash and cash equivalents as presented on the consolidated balance sheet. The Group manages its capital structure and makes adjustments in the light of changes in economic conditions and the risk characteristics of the underlying assets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2021\u163\'00\'A3'000                       2020\u163\'00\'A3'000\par Equity                          \u163\'00\'A3        300,669 \u163\'00\'A3 236,327\par Loans and borrowings            -        -\par Less: Cash and cash equivalents (69,884) (101,327)\par Total Capital                   \u163\'00\'A3        230,785 \u163\'00\'A3 135,000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 33.Subsequent Events\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There were no significant subsequent events from the end of the fiscal year until the date of signing of this report that would require and adjustment to or disclosure in the financial statements.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-70\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SIGNATURES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The registrant hereby certifies that it meets all of t