\par\par \b \uc2 Boston Scientific Corporation\uc2  Recommended Cash Offer for \uc2 BTG plc\b0\par\par\uc2 27,990 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2018\par 09:51\par \uc2 Regulatory News Service\par \uc2 RNS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2018 \par \par \uc2 TIDMBTG\par \par \uc2 RNS Number : 8872H\par \par \uc2 Boston Scientific Corporation\par \par \uc2 20 November 2018\par \par \uc2 NOT FOR RELEASE, PUBLICATION OR DISTRIBUTION IN WHOLE OR IN PART, DIRECTLY OR INDIRECTLY, IN, INTO OR FROM ANY JURISDICTION WHERE TO DO SO WOULD CONSTITUTE A VIOLATION OF THE RELEVANT LAWS OR REGULATIONS OF SUCH JURISDICTION\par \par \uc2 FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\par \par \uc2 THIS ANNOUNCEMENT CONTAINS INSIDE INFORMATION\par \par \uc2 20 November 2018\par \par \uc2 RECOMMENDED CASH OFFER\par \par \uc2 for\par \par \uc2 BTG plc\par \par \uc2 ("\uc2 BTG\uc2 ")\par \par \uc2 by\par \par \uc2 Bravo Bidco Limited\par \par \uc2 ("Bravo Bidco")\par \par \uc2 a newly incorporated entity indirectly wholly-owned by \uc2 Boston Scientific Corporation\uc2  ("\uc2 Boston Scientific\uc2 ")\par \par \uc2 intended to be effected by means of a scheme of arrangement under Part 26 of the Companies Act\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 -- The Boards of \uc2 Boston Scientific\uc2 , Bravo Bidco and \uc2 BTG\uc2  are pleased to announce that they have reached agreement on the terms of a recommended cash offer by Bravo Bidco for the acquisition of the entire issued and to be issued ordinary share capital of \uc2 BTG\uc2  (the "Acquisition"). The Acquisition is intended to be effected by means of a scheme of arrangement under Part 26 of the Companies Act (the "Scheme"). \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --      Under the terms of the Acquisition, BTG Shareholders will be entitled to receive: \par    for each BTG Share:       840 pence in cash (the "Offer Price") \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The Offer Price values the entire issued and to be issued ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  at approximately GBP3.3 billion and represents a premium of approximately:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 o 36.6 per cent. to the closing price of 615 pence per BTG Share on 19 November 2018 (being the last Business Day before this Announcement); and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 o 51.0 per cent. to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  90 trading day volume-weighted average share price for the period ended 19 November 2018 (being the last Business Day before this Announcement).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- If any dividend or other distribution is authorised, declared, made or paid in respect of the BTG Shares on or after the date of this Announcement and prior to the Effective Date, Bravo Bidco reserves the right to reduce the Offer Price by the amount of all or part of any such dividend or other distribution.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Recommendation\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, who have been so advised by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs International\f28 \uc2 \f2 , J.P. Morgan Cazenove and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rothschild & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2  as to the financial terms of the Acquisition, each consider the terms of the Acquisition to be fair and reasonable. In providing their financial advice to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, each of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs International\f28 \uc2 \f2 , J.P. Morgan Cazenove and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rothschild & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2  has taken into account the commercial assessments of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Accordingly, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors intend to recommend unanimously that BTG Shareholders vote (or procure the voting) in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the Resolution to be proposed at the General Meeting (or, in the event that the Acquisition is implemented by way of a Takeover Offer, to accept or procure acceptance of the Takeover Offer), as each BTG Director holding BTG Shares has irrevocably undertaken to do in respect of their entire beneficial holdings of 969,032 BTG Shares, representing in aggregate approximately 0.3 per cent. of the issued ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  on the Last Practicable Date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Irrevocable Undertakings and Support for the Acquisition\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- In addition to the irrevocable undertakings received from \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors holding BTG Shares referred to above, Bravo Bidco has received irrevocable undertakings to vote (or to procure the voting) in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the Resolution to be proposed at the General Meeting (or, in the event that the Acquisition is implemented by way of a Takeover Offer, to accept or procure acceptance of the Takeover Offer) from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Invesco Asset Management Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Novo Holdings A/S and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Woodford Investment Management Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  in respect of a total of 127,062,586 BTG Shares, representing, in aggregate, approximately 32.8 per cent. of the share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  in issue on the Last Practicable Date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- In aggregate, therefore, Bravo Bidco has received irrevocable undertakings in respect of 128,031,618 BTG Shares, representing approximately 33.1 per cent. of the share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  in issue on the Last Practicable Date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Further details of these irrevocable undertakings are set out in Appendix III to this Announcement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Comments on the Acquisition\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commenting on the Acquisition, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Michael F. Mahoney\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Boston Scientific said:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The acquisition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  and its rapidly growing peripheral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  portfolio is an exciting extension of our category leadership strategy that will augment our capabilities in important areas of unmet need such as cancer and pulmonary embolism. We are confident that the addition of these therapies to our portfolio will ultimately advance patient care in ways that could not be realised by either company alone, while also allowing us to realise substantial synergies and provide a strong return for investors."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commenting on the Acquisition, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Garry Watts\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the Chairman of BTG said:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Under the leadership of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Louise Makin\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the broader management team, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  has developed into a global healthcare company with a leading \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine platform. We believe \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's offer represents an attractive proposition for BTG Shareholders with a significant premium in cash and recognises the value created by the support of our long term large shareholders. We are proud of what \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  has become and of all \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  employees for their contributions."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commenting on the Acquisition, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Louise Makin\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the Chief Executive Officer of BTG said:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I would like to thank and acknowledge all \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  colleagues for building a leading global healthcare company. Our \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine portfolio delivers value to patients and is a significant growth driver for the business, and we're also proud of our highly profitable pharmaceuticals business focused on critical care products.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We remain committed to transforming patient care through our passion for people, relentless curiosity, and ambition to lead the way. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  shares that vision, and their comprehensive clinical and commercial expertise will accelerate the delivery of our strategy and expand the global reach of our \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine portfolio. The strong strategic and cultural fit between the companies gives me confidence that our business will continue to make a real difference for our patients, customers, employees and wider stakeholders."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is intended that the Acquisition will be implemented by means of the Scheme, further details of which are contained in the full text of this Announcement and will be set out in the Scheme Document. However, Bravo Bidco reserves the right, with the consent of the Panel and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  (or, in certain circumstances, without the consent of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 ), in each case subject to the terms of the Co-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Agreement, to implement the Acquisition by way of a Takeover Offer.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The Acquisition will be subject to the Conditions and certain further terms set out in Appendix I to this Announcement, including, amongst other things:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 o the approval by a majority in number of Scheme Shareholders representing at least 75 per cent. in value of Scheme Shares present, entitled to vote and voting, either in person or by proxy, at the Court Meeting;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 o the approval of the Resolution in connection with the implementation of the Scheme by the requisite majority of BTG Shareholders at the General Meeting;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 o the sanction of the Scheme by the Court;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 o the Scheme becoming Effective by no later than the Long Stop Date;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 o the receipt of competition clearance (or the expiration or termination of any waiting period, as applicable) in the US under the HSR Act;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 o either a CMA decision not to make a CMA Phase 2 Reference or the absence of a CMA request to submit a Merger Notice or an indication from the CMA that the Initial Period has begun when all other Conditions are met; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 o the receipt of merger control clearance (or the expiration or termination of any waiting period, as applicable) in Germany under the German Act Against Restraints of Competition, in Spain under the Spanish Competition Act, or alternatively, in case of a referral under Article 22 of EU Merger Regulation from a member state to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  in the EU.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Scheme Document will include further information about the Acquisition and the Scheme, together with notices of the Court Meeting and the General Meeting and the expected timetable of the Scheme, and will specify the actions to be taken by BTG Shareholders. The Scheme Document will be sent to BTG Shareholders as soon as reasonably practicable and, in any event (save with the consent of the Panel), within 28 days of this Announcement and will be made available on \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.btgplc.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.btgplc.com}}}\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://investors.bostonscientific.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://investors.bostonscientific.com/}}}\uc2 \f2  (subject to certain restrictions in relation to persons in Restricted Jurisdictions).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Scheme is expected to be Effective around mid-2019, subject to the satisfaction or (where applicable) waiver of the Conditions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This summary should be read in conjunction with, and is subject to, the full text of this Announcement (including its Appendices).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  Recommended Cash -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Acquisition will be subject to the Conditions and certain further terms set out in Appendix I and the full terms and conditions which will be set out in the Scheme Document. Appendix II contains the sources of information and bases of calculation of certain information contained in this Announcement. Appendix III contains a summary of the irrevocable undertakings received in relation to the Acquisition, and Appendix IV contains definitions of certain terms and expressions used in this Announcement. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Enquiries: \par Bravo Bidco / \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par  Susie Lisa (Investor Relations)                +1 (508) 683-5565 \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  (financial adviser to Bravo Bidco \par  and Boston Scientific) \par  Doug Solomon \par  Jed Brody \par  Derek Shakespeare                              +44 20 7623 2323 \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 Andy Burrows\f28 \uc2 \f2  (Vice President, Corporate & \par  Investor Relations)                            +44 20 7575 1741 \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs International\f28 \uc2 \f2  (joint financial \par  adviser to BTG) \par  Anthony Gutman \par  Nimesh Khiroya \par  S\u248\'00\'F8ren Moller-Rasmussen                    +44 20 7774 1000 \par J.P. Morgan Cazenove (joint financial adviser \par  and joint corporate broker to BTG) \par  James Mitford \par  Dwayne Lysaght \par  Alex Bruce                                     +44 20 7742 4000 \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rothschild & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2  (joint financial adviser \par  to BTG) \par  Richard Murley \par  Dominic Hollamby \par  Julian Hudson                                  +44 20 7280 5000 \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  (joint corporate broker \par  to BTG) \par  Neil Collingridge \par  Seth Damergy                                   +44 20 7545 8000 \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 FTI Consulting\f28 \uc2 \f2  (PR adviser to BTG) \par  Ben Atwell                                     +44 20 3727 1000 