\uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  or Bravo Bidco for any period and no statement in this Announcement should be interpreted to mean that cash flow from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , earnings, or earnings per share or income of those persons (where relevant) for the current or future financial years would necessarily match or exceed the historical published cash flow from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , earnings, earnings per share or income of those persons (as appropriate).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Disclosure requirements of the Code\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Under Rule 8.3(a) of the Code, any person who is interested in 1 per cent. or more of any class of relevant securities of an offeree company or of any securities exchange offeror (being any offeror other than an offeror in respect of which it has been announced that its offer is, or is likely to be, solely in cash) must make an Opening Position Disclosure following the commencement of the Offer Period and, if later, following the Announcement in which any securities exchange offeror is first identified. An Opening Position Disclosure must contain details of the person's interests and short positions in, and rights to subscribe for, any relevant securities of each of (i) the offeree company and (ii) any securities exchange offeror(s). An Opening Position Disclosure by a person to whom Rule 8.3(a) applies must be made by no later than 3:30 pm (London time) on the 10(th) Business Day following the commencement of the Offer Period and, if appropriate, by no later than 3:30 pm (London time) on the 10(th) Business Day following the Announcement in which any securities exchange offeror is first identified. Relevant persons who deal in the relevant securities of the offeree company or of a securities exchange offeror prior to the deadline for making an Opening Position Disclosure must instead make a Dealing Disclosure.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Under Rule 8.3(b) of the Code, any person who is, or becomes, interested in 1 per cent. or more of any class of relevant securities of the offeree company or of any securities exchange offeror must make a Dealing Disclosure if the person deals in any relevant securities of the offeree company or of any securities exchange offeror. A Dealing Disclosure must contain details of the dealing concerned and of the person's interests and short positions in, and rights to subscribe for, any relevant securities of each of (i) the offeree company and (ii) any securities exchange offeror, save to the extent that these details have previously been disclosed under Rule 8. A Dealing Disclosure by a person to whom Rule 8.3(b) applies must be made by no later than 3.30 pm (London time) on the Business Day following the date of the relevant dealing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If two or more persons act together pursuant to an agreement or understanding, whether formal or informal, to acquire or control an interest in relevant securities of an offeree company or a securities exchange offeror, they will normally be deemed to be a single person for the purpose of Rule 8.3.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Opening Position Disclosures must also be made by the offeree company and by any offeror and Dealing Disclosures must also be made by the offeree company, by any offeror and by any persons acting in concert with any of them (see Rules 8.1, 8.2 and 8.4). Details of the offeree and offeror companies in respect of whose relevant securities Opening Position Disclosures and Dealing Disclosures must be made can be found in the Disclosure Table on the Panel's website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.thetakeoverpanel.org.uk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.thetakeoverpanel.org.uk}}}\uc2 \f2 , including details of the number of relevant securities in issue, when the Offer Period commenced and when any offeror was first identified. You should contact the Panel's Market Surveillance Unit on +44 (0)20 7638 0129 if you are in any doubt as to whether you are required to make an Opening Position Disclosure or a Dealing Disclosure.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Information relating to BTG Shareholders\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Please note that addresses, electronic addresses (if any) and certain other information provided by BTG Shareholders, persons with information rights and other relevant persons for the receipt of communications from \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  may be provided to Bravo Bidco during the Offer Period as required under Section 4 of Appendix 4 of the Code.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Publication on website and availability of hard copies\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This Announcement and the display documents required to be published pursuant to Rule 26.1 of the Code will be made available, free of charge and subject to certain restrictions relating to persons in Restricted Jurisdictions, on \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.btgplc.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.btgplc.com}}}\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://investors.bostonscientific.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://investors.bostonscientific.com/}}}\uc2 \f2  by no later than 12 noon (London time) on the Business Day following the date of this Announcement. For the avoidance of doubt, neither the content of such website nor the content of any other website accessible from hyperlinks on such websites is incorporated into, nor forms part of, this Announcement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In accordance with Rule 30.3 of the Code, a person so entitled may request a copy of this Announcement (and any information incorporated into it by reference to another source) in hard copy form by writing to Link Asset Services, The Registry, 34 Beckenham Road, Beckenham, Kent BR3 4TU or by calling them on 0871 664 0300 from within the UK or on +44 3716640300 from outside the UK. Such person may also request that all future documents announcements and information sent to that person in relation to the Acquisition should be in hard copy form. Save as otherwise referred to above, a hard copy of this Announcement will not be sent unless requested.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Relevant securities in issue\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In accordance with Rule 2.9 of the Code, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  confirms that, as at the close of business on 19 November 2018, it has 387,150,467 ordinary shares of 10 pence each in issue admitted to trading on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 's market for listed securities. The International Securities Identification Number for BTG Shares is GB0001001592.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If you are in any doubt about the contents of this Announcement or the action you should take, you are recommended to seek your own independent financial advice immediately from your stockbroker, bank manager, solicitor or independent financial adviser duly authorised under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (as amended) if you are resident in the United Kingdom or, if not, from another appropriate authorised independent financial adviser.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NOT FOR RELEASE, PUBLICATION OR DISTRIBUTION IN WHOLE OR IN PART, DIRECTLY OR INDIRECTLY, IN, INTO OR FROM ANY JURISDICTION WHERE TO DO SO WOULD CONSTITUTE A VIOLATION OF THE RELEVANT LAWS OR REGULATIONS OF SUCH JURISDICTION\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 THE ANNOUNCEMENT CONTAINS INSIDE INFORMATION\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 20 November 2018\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RECOMMENDED CASH OFFER\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BTG plc\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ("\f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 ")\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 by\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bravo Bidco Limited\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ("Bravo Bidco")\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a newly incorporated entity indirectly wholly-owned by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  ("\f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 ")\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 intended to be effected by means of a scheme of arrangement under Part 26 of the Companies Act \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    1.             Introduction \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Boards of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Bravo Bidco and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  are pleased to announce that they have reached agreement on the terms of a recommended cash offer by Bravo Bidco for the acquisition of the entire issued and to be issued ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  (the "Acquisition"). The Acquisition is intended to be effected by means of a scheme of arrangement under Part 26 of the Companies Act (the "Scheme"). \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    2.             The Acquisition \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Under the terms of the Acquisition, which will be subject to the Conditions and further terms set out in Appendix I to this Announcement and to be set out in the Scheme Document, BTG Shareholders will be entitled to receive: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    for each BTG Share:                     840 pence in cash (the "Offer Price") \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Offer Price values the entire issued and to be issued ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  at approximately GBP3.3 billion and represents a premium of approximately:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- 36.6 per cent. to the closing price of 615 pence per BTG Share on 19 November 2018 (being the last Business Day before this Announcement); and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- 51.0 per cent. to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  90 trading day volume-weighted average share price for the period ended 19 November 2018 (being the last Business Day before this Announcement).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BTG Shares to be acquired under the Acquisition will be acquired fully paid and free from all liens, charges, equitable interests, encumbrances, rights of pre-emption and any other rights and interests of any nature whatsoever and together with all rights now and hereafter attaching thereto.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If any dividend or other distribution is authorised, declared, made or paid in respect of BTG Shares on or after the date of this Announcement and prior to the Effective Date, Bravo Bidco reserves the right to reduce the Offer Price by the amount of all or part of any such dividend or other distribution. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    3.             Background to and reasons for the Acquisition \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  Recommended Cash -5-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  is one of the largest independent medical technology companies in the world with a wide range of product offerings that address unmet patient needs across multiple medical conditions. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  possesses a long history of growth through internal innovation complemented by selective acquisitions and regularly reviews opportunities for its diverse set of businesses.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  believes that the Acquisition represents a compelling opportunity to build upon the strengths of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's $1.2 billion Peripheral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Division with the addition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's high growth and complementary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  medicine platform.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's pharmaceutical business adds a profitable portfolio of lifesaving acute care drugs, and its licensing business adds a portfolio of profitable licensed pharmaceutical products that generate a stream of royalties with minimal infrastructure requirements.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's comprehensive and global research and development, clinical and commercial expertise combined with \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's strong positions in growing areas of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  oncology and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vascular will position the combined entity to better serve patients, payors and providers around the world.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In particular, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects the Acquisition to deliver short and long-term benefits, including:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- strengthening \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's offerings in the area of cancer treatment with the addition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's highly differentiated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  oncology segment that will enable \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  to expand treatment options for cancer patients worldwide;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- advancing \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's category leadership strategy in the Peripheral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  segment by adding high growth revenues ($341 million for the 12 month period ending September 30, 2018) to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's existing Peripheral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Division;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- expanding \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's venous portfolio offering by adding \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's pulmonary embolism franchise in addition to other highly differentiated vascular products;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- providing a strong return to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's investors, including by adding two to three cents of accretion to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's adjusted earnings per share in 2019, and increasing levels of accretion thereafter; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- delivering significant revenue and cost synergies through \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's enhanced global manufacturing capabilities and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's combined geographic footprint.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  is confident in its ability to deliver on its strategy for the Acquisition, having demonstrated a strong track record of integrating acquisitions into its organisation and driving both revenue growth and operating improvements through more than 20 acquisitions in the past five years. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    4.             Background to and reasons for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors' Recommendation \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Since its floatation in 1995, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  has developed into a global specialist healthcare company. Under the leadership of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Louise Makin\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the management team, a key element of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's strategy in the past decade has been to develop a leading and scalable \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine portfolio to bring patients a set of innovative medical technologies enabling minimally invasive, often image guided, procedures. Today \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine portfolio represents a significant growth driver for the business and one of the few well-developed scale platforms in the market. Alongside \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  also benefits from its highly profitable pharmaceuticals business focused on critical care products, as well as royalties from legacy intellectual property licencing arrangements. \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  has delivered a compelling financial performance with revenue, operating profit and adjusted earnings per share growth of 9 per cent., 18 per cent., and 42 per cent., respectively, for the financial year ended 31 March 2018. This strong growth was reinforced in the results for the six month period ended 30 September 2018, which were announced on 13 November 2018. When combined with the continued scaling of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine business and its strong financial profile, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors remain highly confident that the ongoing successful execution of its strategy would provide long-term growth and create significant value for shareholders.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors believe that \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  has a clear strategy and strong independent future. However, following the approach from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors have held detailed discussions regarding the terms of the potential Acquisition. These discussions resulted in the Offer Price of 840 pence in cash for each Ordinary Share.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In assessing the terms of the Acquisition, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors considered the all-cash nature of the consideration, which would provide BTG Shareholders with the opportunity to receive an immediate and certain value in cash, that would otherwise potentially be unlocked over a longer period of time as \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  executes its strategy and realises its longer term potential, whilst taking into account the inherent execution risks. These risks include an uncertain macro and regulatory and reimbursement environment, patent challenges or expiries, potential novel or generic competition on products, potential failure of clinical trials, commercialisation risk on innovation, competition from larger players in various markets and ongoing integration of M&A.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors note: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --      the terms of the Acquisition represents a premium of: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 o approximately 36.6 per cent. to the Closing Price per BTG Share of 615 pence on 19 November 2018 (being the Business Day before this Announcement); and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 o approximately 51.0 per cent. to the 90 trading day volume-weighted average price per BTG Share of 556 pence for the period ended 19 November 2018 (being the Business Day before this Announcement);\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the terms of the Acquisition provide a vehicle for BTG Shareholders to monetise their shares in \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  without suffering an illiquidity discount; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors believe that the terms of the Acquisition provide fair value for BTG Shareholders relative to the standalone prospects of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  or alternative strategies for realising value from the BTG Group's assets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors have also considered the interests of its shareholders, employees, customers and patients. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors believe that under \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's ownership, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  would be able to accelerate the delivery of its strategy and further enhance its growth profile through combining the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine business with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Peripheral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  business and leveraging \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's comprehensive and global clinical and commercial expertise, allowing for the global roll-out of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine portfolio. As part of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  would have the opportunity to benefit from enhanced scale and financial resources, which should enable further innovation to address unmet needs for patients. \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  is also aware of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's track record of successfully integrating businesses and it therefore believes there is a strong strategic and cultural fit with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  for its customers, employees and wider stakeholders. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    5.             Recommendation by \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, who have been so advised by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs International\f28 \uc2 \f2 , J.P. Morgan Cazenove and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rothschild & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2  as to the financial terms of the Acquisition, each consider the terms of the Acquisition to be fair and reasonable. In providing their financial advice to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, each of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs International\f28 \uc2 \f2 , J.P. Morgan Cazenove and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rothschild & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2  has taken into account the commercial assessments of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Accordingly, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors intend to recommend unanimously that BTG Shareholders vote (or procure the voting) in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the Resolution to be proposed at the General Meeting (or in the event that the Acquisition is implemented by way of a Takeover Offer, to accept or procure acceptance of the Takeover Offer), as each BTG Director holding BTG Shares has irrevocably undertaken to do in respect of their entire beneficial holdings of 969,032 BTG Shares, in aggregate, representing approximately 0.3 per cent. of the issued ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  on the Last Practicable Date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Further details of these irrevocable undertakings are set out in Appendix III to this Announcement. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    6.             Irrevocable Undertakings and Support for the Acquisition from other BTG Shareholders \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition to the irrevocable undertakings received from \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors referred to above, Bravo Bidco has received irrevocable undertakings to vote (or to procure the voting) in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the Resolution to be proposed at the General Meeting (or, in the event that the Acquisition is implemented by way of a Takeover Offer, to accept or procure acceptance of the Takeover Offer) from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Invesco Asset Management Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Novo Holdings A/S and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Woodford Investment Management Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  in respect of a total of 127,062,586 BTG Shares, representing, in aggregate, approximately 32.8 per cent. of the share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  in issue on the Last Practicable Date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In aggregate, therefore, Bravo Bidco has received irrevocable undertakings in respect of 128,031,618 BTG Shares, representing approximately 33.1 per cent. of the share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  in issue on the Last Practicable Date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Further details of these irrevocable undertakings are set out in Appendix III to this Announcement. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    7.             Conditions to the Acquisition \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Acquisition will be subject to the Conditions and certain further terms set out in Appendix I to this Announcement, including:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the approval by a majority in number of Scheme Shareholders representing at least 75 per cent. in value of Scheme Shares present, entitled to vote and voting, either in person or by proxy, at the Court Meeting;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  Recommended Cash -6-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the approval of the Resolution in connection with the implementation of the Scheme by the requisite majority of BTG Shareholders at the General Meeting; \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --      the sanction of the Scheme by the Court; \par    --      the Scheme becoming Effective by no later than the Long Stop Date; \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the receipt of competition clearance (or the expiration or termination of any waiting period, as applicable) in the US under the HSR Act;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- either a CMA decision not to make a CMA Phase 2 Reference or the absence of a CMA request to submit a Merger Notice or an indication from the CMA that the Initial Period has begun when all other Conditions are met; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the receipt of merger control clearance (or the expiration or termination of any waiting period, as applicable) in Germany under the German Act Against Restraints of Competition, in Spain under the Spanish Competition Act, or alternatively, in case of a referral under Article 22 of EU Merger Regulation from a member state to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  in the EU. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    8.             Information on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Bravo Bidco \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 , based in Marlborough, Massachusetts, transforms lives through innovative solutions that improve the health of patients around the world. For nearly 40 years, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  has advanced science for life by providing a broad range of high performance solutions that address unmet patient needs and reduce the cost of healthcare.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With annual sales approaching $10 billion, a market capitalisation around $50 billion and a strong investment grade credit rating, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  is one of the largest independent medical technology companies in the world. It carries on its business through three operating segments that comprise seven franchises; MedSurg (Endoscopy, Urology & Pelvic Health), Rhythm & Neuro (CRM, Electrophysiology and Neuromodulation) and Cardiovascular (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Cardiology and Peripheral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ). \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  has a long history of growth through internal innovation and successful acquisitions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bravo Bidco is a newly incorporated indirectly wholly-owned subsidiary of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  formed for the purpose of implementing the Acquisition. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    9.             Information on \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 , headquartered in London, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 United Kingdom\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , is a global healthcare company focused on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine, with a fast-growing Oncology and Vascular portfolio to advance the treatment of cancer, blood clots and varicose veins through minimally invasive procedures. Alongside \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  has a cash-generative Pharmaceuticals business that provides life-saving products to treat patients overexposed to certain medications or toxins. Inspired by patient and physician needs, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  is expanding its portfolio to address some of today's most complex healthcare challenges.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  was formed in 1981 from the merger of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 UK government\f28 \uc2 \f2 's National Research & Development Council and National Enterprise Board. Since its flotation on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  in 1995, the group has built the capabilities and infrastructure to support ongoing business growth globally. \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  has a significant direct commercial presence in Europe and the US, supporting the group's growth and geographic expansion. \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  continues to develop its product portfolio through investments in pipeline innovation and clinical studies, as well as through a focused acquisition strategy. \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  operates two businesses: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine and Pharmaceuticals. It also receives royalties from legacy Licensing activities.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine: \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  is a leader in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine therapies, the fast growing field of minimally invasive, often image-guided procedures used to treat a range of conditions, focused on Oncology and Vascular segments. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Oncology offers treatments for a variety of cancers and tumours. Key products include TheraSphere(R), glass microspheres that deliver internal radiation therapy; LC Bead(R) and DC Bead(R), embolization and chemoebolization polymer beads; and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  cryoablation systems. This unique portfolio gives \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  the ability to offer customers minimally invasive treatment alternatives to systemic radiotherapy, chemotherapy or open surgery. The Vascular portfolio focuses on the treatment of blood clots and varicose veins. Key products include EKOS(R), an ultrasonic device to help dissolve blood clots, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  crossing devices, anchoring catheters used to cross complex lesions, and venous filters, as well as Varithena(R), an injectable microfoam for the treatment of varicose veins.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pharmaceuticals: \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's products are used in hospital emergency rooms and intensive care units. The products typically address conditions with small patient populations for which there are limited or no existing treatment options. Key products within the pharmaceuticals portfolio include CroFab(R), DigiFab(R) and Voraxaze(R) that are used respectively for the treatment of envenomation by certain snakes and overexposure to particular heart and cancer medications.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Licensing: in addition to generating revenues from its own products, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  earns royalties on products sold by its licensees. Licensed products include Zytiga(R), licensed to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Johnson & Johnson\f28 \uc2 \f2  and used for the treatment of prostate cancer, and the Two-Part Hip Cup, a prosthetic hip joint replacement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the six months ended 30 September 2018 (the "1H 2018/19 Fiscal Year"), \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  generated sales of $495.7m (+12% vs six months ended 30 September 2017 (the "1H 2017/18 Fiscal Year")) of which $340.2m was from product sales (+10% vs 1H 2017/18 Fiscal Year) and $155.5m from licensing revenues (+18% vs 1H 2017/18 Fiscal Year). Group adjusted profit was $178.5m (+39% vs 1H 2017/18 Fiscal Year) representing a 36% adjusted profit margin. For 1H 2018/19 Fiscal Year \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine generated $172.3m (+12% vs 1H 2018 Fiscal Year), of which $110.9m was from Oncology (+12% vs 1H 2017/18 Fiscal Year) and $59.2m from Vascular (+20% vs 1H 2017/18 Fiscal year) while Pharmaceuticals generated $167.9m (+7% vs 1H 20/1718 Fiscal Year). Net cash and cash equivalents was $285.2m as at 30 September 2018.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On 4 October 2018, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  announced that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Garry Watts\f28 \uc2 \f2  had informed the BTG Board that he wished to retire as Chairman and as a non-executive director of BTG at the end of 2018. Given the Acquisition, it is now expected that he will remain as Chairman and as a non-executive director until the Effective Date. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    10.          Post-Offer Intentions with regard to the Business, Employees and Pension Schemes \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  values \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's culture, reputation with customers, its commitment to quality and its focus on addressing unmet patient needs through innovation and product excellence. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  have highly complementary businesses in the area of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  medicine. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to apply the combined group's expertise across therapeutic areas, research and development capabilities, and all employee talents to provide innovative solutions for patients, benefits for stakeholders and growth for shareholders.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's due diligence review of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  has primarily consisted of a detailed review of publicly available information regarding \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 , since it signed a Confidentiality Agreement with \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  on 31 October 2018, limited interactions with a narrow group of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's senior management, and review of the limited materials provided to it by \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 , because of its own Peripheral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  business and its track record of acquiring and integrating other businesses, also is familiar with businesses similar to \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's and the integration process. Based on this review, its industry and transactional experience, and its own Peripheral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  business, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  believes there will be meaningful duplication of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  infrastructure between the two businesses, primarily in the area of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  has not yet received sufficiently detailed information to formulate comprehensive plans or intentions regarding the impact of the Acquisition on \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  and, accordingly, intends to take a 'best of both' approach in optimising the operating structure of the combined Peripheral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  business.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  possesses extensive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around the world, including its global headquarters in Marlborough, Massachusetts, which it will retain following the completion of the Acquisition, and a significant \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  presence in Maple Grove, Minnesota. It expects to realise synergies from the Acquisition by eliminating duplication across functions, including eliminating \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's public company infrastructure and listing costs. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  also expects to eliminate other duplicative general and administrative costs, including by reducing headcount and by combining or relocating \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's remaining head office functions with or to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  facilities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  also expects to realise synergies by increasing manufacturing and supply chain efficiencies, which are expected to include reduction of manufacturing footprint by re-deploying or disposing of fixed assets. Whether these fixed assets will be re-deployed or disposed of will depend on the nature of these assets, including how efficient they are. As part of its post-closing evaluation, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  will also review \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's research and development activities. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects to conduct this review promptly after completion of the Acquisition with the goal of identifying \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's promising pipeline projects and duplicative facilities and headcount. Following completion of this review, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects to preserve and enhance the development of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's promising pipeline products and to eliminate less promising pipeline products, as well as duplicative facilities and headcount.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  Recommended Cash -7-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects to implement expense reductions across a range of operating functions in the combined Peripheral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  business. Based on its limited due diligence to date, it does not yet have sufficient information to be able to estimate with specificity the extent or location of these reductions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Based on its experience integrating other acquired businesses, subject to complying with applicable laws, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects to be able to begin to develop detailed steps for the integration of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  businesses in the period prior to the completion of the Acquisition, and to finalise its integration plan within six to nine months after completion of the Acquisition.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  also expects to realise revenue synergies in its Peripheral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Medicine businesses by driving incremental top-line growth through a larger combined, global commercial team and by leveraging \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's significant presence outside the United States.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Based on the limited information it has received to date and its experience integrating other acquired companies and operating similar businesses, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects to realise annual cost and revenue synergies of approximately US $175 million by the end of 2021, largely consisting of cost synergies, a significant portion of which are expected to come from headcount reductions. Because of the limited due diligence \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  has been permitted to conduct to date, and its intention to take a "best of both" approach to integration, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  cannot yet say what the total number of headcount reduction will be or the proportion of the expected headcount reductions that will come from \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  or from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 . If a large portion of the headcount reductions were to come from \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 , they would be material to \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  has yet to formulate its long-term plans with respect to BTG's Pharmaceuticals business. In the meantime, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  intends to operate this business in substantially the same manner as it is currently operated.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The finalisation and implementation of any workforce reductions will be subject to comprehensive planning and engagement with employees and consultation with employee representatives as required by applicable local law. Any affected employees will be treated in a fair and equitable manner consistent with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's high standards and culture of respect.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  has agreed that, in implementing any headcount reductions, it would enhance that part of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's existing US severance policy that relates to minimum severance payments and make it applicable to both US and non-US employees so that \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's general employees (i.e. employees below management other than professional and sales employees) would receive a minimum of ten weeks' pay (including pay for any notice period), and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's professional and sales employees would receive a minimum of 14 weeks' pay (including pay for any notice period). Severance payments would be paid in a lump sum rather than as salary continuation as is currently provided under \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's US severance policy. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  intends to approach employee integration with the aim of retaining and motivating the best talent across the combined company to further enhance a high performance organisation. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  intends to inform all \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  employees as to whether they will have permanent positions going forward as soon as reasonably practicable following completion of the Acquisition.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  confirms that it has given assurances to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors that upon and following completion of the Acquisition, it intends to fully observe the existing contractual employment rights, including pension rights, of all \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  management and employees. In addition, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  has committed that, for the first twelve months after completion of the Acquisition, the terms and conditions of employment of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  employees will be no less favourable (taking into account salary and benefits) than their existing terms and conditions of employment, except that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  will provide incentive compensation arrangements to \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  employees that are consistent with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's compensation schemes, having regard to \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's current incentive arrangements and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's desire to attract and retain \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's talented employees.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  has also stated its intention to put in place retention arrangements for certain of its employees, under which it is expected that it will make additional cash retention awards in an aggregate amount of up to GBP18 million to employees whose retention is considered by \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 , following consultation with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  in certain cases, to be critical for achieving the successful completion of the Acquisition and business continuity through and following the completion of the Acquisition.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subject to the assurances \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  has provided to \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  as described above, following the completion of the Acquisition, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects to migrate all \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's management and employees on to the standard terms, conditions and benefits offered to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's management and employees, such that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's management and employees are treated equally. However, except as otherwise required by applicable law, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not provide pension benefits to its employees. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  has not yet had sufficient access to \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's benefit plans to be able to determine whether this migration will commence within the first 12 months after completion of the Acquisition or after this 12-month period. Pending this migration, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not intend to make any changes with regard to employer contributions to \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's existing pension schemes or the accrual of benefits to existing members or the admission of new members to such pension schemes. Subject to the potential headcount reductions described herein, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not intend to make any material changes to the balance of the skills and functions of the employees and management of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 No statements in this Paragraph 10 constitute "post-offer undertakings" for the purposes of Rule 19.5 of the Code. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    11.          Financing arrangements \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  will provide Bravo Bidco with the cash consideration to be paid to BTG Shareholders pursuant to the Acquisition from new third party borrowing by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  to be entered into prior to the Effective Date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For cash confirmation purposes, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  has obtained a bridge facility from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Bank PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  for the full amount of the cash consideration required. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  has committed to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  to provide Bravo Bidco with the cash consideration to be paid to the BTG Shareholders pursuant to the Acquisition.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Under the terms of such bridge facility, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  has agreed that it will not amend, treat as satisfied or waive any term or condition without the consent of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Bank PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  as lead arranger (such consent not to be unreasonably withheld, conditioned or delayed) if to do so would be materially adverse to the interests of the lenders under the relevant credit agreement, save as required pursuant to the City Code, the Panel, a competent regulatory authority or by the Court.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2 , in its capacity as financial adviser to Bravo Bidco and Boston Scientific, is satisfied that resources available to Bravo Bidco are sufficient to satisfy, in full, the cash consideration payable to BTG Shareholders under the terms of the Acquisition. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    12.          Structure of the Acquisition and the Scheme Document \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Scheme\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is intended that the Acquisition will be effected by a Court-sanctioned scheme of arrangement between \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the Scheme Shareholders under Part 26 of the Companies Act. The intention of the Scheme is to enable Bravo Bidco to become the owner of the whole of the issued and to be issued share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Under the Scheme, the Scheme Shares will be transferred to Bravo Bidco and in consideration the Scheme Shareholders will receive the consideration on the basis set out in paragraph 2 of this Announcement. The Scheme will be subject to the Conditions and further terms and conditions referred to in Appendix I to this Announcement and to be set out in the Scheme Document. The Acquisition will lapse if the Scheme does not become Effective by the Long Stop Date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Approval by the Court Meeting and the General Meeting\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In order to become Effective, the Scheme requires the approval of the Scheme Shareholders by the passing of a resolution at the Court Meeting. The resolution must be approved by a majority in number of the Scheme Shareholders present and voting and entitled to vote, either in person or by proxy, representing not less than 75 per cent. in value of the Scheme Shares held by such Scheme Shareholders. At the Court Meeting, voting will be by poll and not on a show of hands.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition, a special resolution must be passed at the General Meeting to approve amendments to \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's articles of association to ensure that any BTG Shares issued after the approval of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the Scheme Record Time will be: (i) subject to the Scheme; and (ii) automatically acquired by Bravo Bidco on the same terms as under the Scheme), which requires the approval of BTG Shareholders representing at least 75 per cent. of the votes cast at the General Meeting (either in person or by proxy). The General Meeting will be held immediately after the Court Meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Application to the Court to sanction the Scheme\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Once the necessary approvals have been obtained at the BTG Meetings, and the other Conditions (save for the Conditions set out at paragraphs 1(c) and (d) of Part A of Appendix I to this Announcement) have been satisfied or (where applicable) waived, in order for the Scheme to be capable of becoming Effective, it must be sanctioned by the Court at the Scheme Court Hearing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Scheme will only become Effective on delivery of the Scheme Court Order to the Registrar of Companies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Scheme becoming Effective\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  Recommended Cash -8-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subject to the satisfaction or (where applicable) waiver of the Conditions, the Scheme is expected to become Effective around mid-2019.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Upon the Scheme becoming Effective, it will be binding on all Scheme Shareholders, irrespective of whether or not they attended or voted at the Court Meeting or General Meeting, or whether they voted in favour of or against the Scheme.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Offer Price will be despatched by Bravo Bidco to Scheme Shareholders no later than 14 days after the Effective Date. Share certificates in respect of BTG Shares will cease to be valid and entitlements to BTG Shares held within the CREST system will be cancelled.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Scheme Document\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Scheme Document will include full details of the Scheme, together with notices of the Court Meeting and the General Meeting and the expected timetable for the Scheme, and will specify the action to be taken by BTG Shareholders.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is expected that the Scheme Document, together with the Forms of Proxy, will be despatched to BTG Shareholders and, for information only, to participants in the BTG Share Plans as soon as reasonably practicable.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Scheme will be governed by the laws of England and Wales. The Scheme will be also subject to the applicable requirements of the Code, the Panel, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Financial Conduct Authority\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    13.          Disclosure of interests in BTG Shares \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As at close of business on the Last Practicable Date, save for the irrevocable undertakings referred to in Sections 5 and 6 of this Announcement, none of Bravo Bidco, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  or any of their respective directors, or, so far as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  is aware, any persons acting in concert (as such term is defined in the Code) with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  had: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --      any interest in, or right to subscribe for, any relevant securities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- any short position in (whether conditional or absolute and whether in the money or otherwise), including any short position under a derivative, any agreement to sell or any delivery obligation or right to require another person to purchase or take delivery of, relevant securities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 ;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- procured an irrevocable commitment or letter of intent to accept the terms of the Acquisition in respect of relevant securities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; or \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --      borrowed or lent any such securities. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Furthermore, save for the irrevocable undertakings described in Sections 5 and 6 of this Announcement, no arrangement exists between \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Bravo Bidco or any person acting in concert (as such term is defined in the Code) with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  or Bravo Bidco and any other person in relation to BTG Shares. For these purposes, an arrangement includes any indemnity or option arrangement, any agreement or understanding, formal or informal, of whatever nature, relating to BTG Shares which may be an inducement to deal or refrain from dealing in such securities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the interests of maintaining confidentiality, it has not been possible for Bravo Bidco to complete its enquiries in respect of the interests in BTG Shares (if any) of all of Bravo Bidco's concert parties in advance of the release of this Announcement. Enquiries of such parties will be completed as soon as practicable following the date of this Announcement. In accordance with Note 2(a)(i) on Rule 8 of the Code, further disclosures, if any, required in respect of such parties will be made as soon as possible and in any event by no later than 12 noon (London time) on the date falling 10 Business Days after the date of this Announcement. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    14.          BTG Share Plans \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Participants in the BTG Share Plans will be contacted regarding the effect of the Acquisition on their rights under the BTG Share Plans and appropriate proposals will be made to such participants in due course. Further details of the terms of such proposals will be included in the Scheme Document and separate proposal documentation. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    15.          Acquisition-related Arrangements \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Confidentiality agreement\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On 31 October 2018, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  entered into a confidentiality agreement in relation to the Acquisition, pursuant to which \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  undertook to keep information related to \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  confidential and to not disclose it to third parties (other than to permitted persons) unless required by law or regulation. Unless terminated earlier, the confidentiality obligations will remain in force for five years from the date of the agreement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The confidentiality agreement also contains undertakings from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  that, for a period of 12 months from the date of the confidentiality agreement and subject to customary carve outs, neither \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  nor \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  shall employ or seek to employ certain employees of the other.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Co-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Agreement\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Bravo Bidco and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  have entered into the Co-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Agreement pursuant to which:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Bravo Bidco have each agreed to use commercially reasonable efforts to secure certain regulatory clearances and to satisfy certain regulatory conditions as promptly as possible following the date of the Co-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Agreement and, in any event, by the Long Stop Date. Commercially reasonable efforts: (a) shall include divestiture of either the Boston Scientific Bead Business or the BTG Bead Business, provided that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  has up to three months following \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  submitting a filing pursuant to the HSR Act to make the case to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 US Federal Trade Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  or \f28 \uc2 \f2 US Department of Justice\f28 \uc2 \f2  prior to offering such divestiture; and (b) shall preclude \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  or Bravo Bidco from committing to effect any transaction that would be reasonably likely to preclude or materially impede or prejudice the effectiveness of any application for any such regulatory clearance;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Bravo Bidco and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  have each undertaken to, among other things, provide information and assistance in relation to filings, notifications or submissions to be made in connection with implementing the Acquisition and obtaining certain regulatory clearances; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Bravo Bidco have each undertaken to provide information and assistance in connection with the preparation of the Scheme Document and implementation of the Scheme.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Co-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Agreement records Bravo Bidco's and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's intention to implement the Acquisition by way of a Scheme, subject to the ability of Bravo Bidco to implement the Acquisition by way of a Takeover Offer in the circumstances described in the Co-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Agreement. The parties have agreed that where \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  consents to Bravo Bidco implementing the Acquisition by way of a Takeover Offer, the acceptance condition to the Takeover Offer shall be set at not more than 75 per cent. of the BTG Shares to which the Takeover Offer Relates. The Co-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Agreement contains provisions in relation to the BTG Share Schemes and to the treatment of employees as summarised in Section 10 above.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Co-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Agreement will terminate if: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --      agreed in writing between \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Bravo Bidco and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- upon service of written notice from Bravo Bidco to \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  if: (a) the Scheme Document does not contain the BTG Recommendation; (b) the BTG Board withdraws or adversely modifies or qualifies the BTG Recommendation; (c) \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  makes an announcement before publication of the Scheme Document that it will not convene the Court Meeting or the General Meeting or that it intends not to post the Scheme Document (otherwise than as a result of the Acquisition being implemented by way of a Takeover Offer); or (d) a competing transaction is announced and such competing transaction is recommended by the BTG Board;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- upon service of written notice from Bravo Bidco to \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  or \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  to Bravo Bidco, the Effective Date has not occurred on or prior to the Long Stop Date; or \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --      a competing transaction completes, becomes effective or unconditional in all respects; or \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- any Condition has been invoked, with the consent of the Panel, and the Scheme has been withdrawn, or if the Acquisition is to be implemented by way of a Takeover Offer, the Takeover Offer lapses. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    16.          Delisting and cancellation of trading and re-registration \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is intended that dealings in BTG Shares will be suspended shortly before the Effective Date at a time to be set out in the Scheme Document. It is further intended that applications will be made to: (a) the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  to cancel trading in BTG Shares on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 's main market for listed securities; and (b) the UK Listing Authority to cancel the listing of the BTG Shares on the Daily Official List, in each case with effect from or shortly after the Effective Date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The last day of dealing in BTG Shares on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  is currently expected to be the Business Day immediately prior to the Effective Date and it is currently intended that no transfers will be registered after 6:00 pm on that date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Share certificates in respect of the BTG Shares will cease to be valid and should be destroyed on the Effective Date. In addition, entitlements held within CREST to BTG Shares will be cancelled on the Effective Date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is Bravo Bidco's intention that in due course, following a delisting, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  will be re-registered as a private limited company. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    17.          Overseas shareholders \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The distribution of this Announcement to persons not resident in the United Kingdom and/or the ability of such persons to vote on the Acquisition at the BTG Meetings (or, if the Acquisition is implemented by way of a Takeover Offer, to accept such Takeover Offer) may be prohibited or affected by the laws of the relevant jurisdictions in which such persons are resident. Such persons should inform themselves about, and observe, any applicable requirements.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  Recommended Cash -9-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Further details in relation to overseas BTG Shareholders will be contained in the Scheme Document. BTG Shareholders who are in any doubt about such matters should consult an appropriate independent professional adviser in the relevant jurisdiction without delay. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    18.          BTG ADRs \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BTG Shares underlying the BTG ADRs will be included in the Acquisition. BTG ADR holders should contact the depositary for their BTG ADRs for information regarding their rights. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    19.          Documents on display \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following documents will be published on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://investors.bostonscientific.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://investors.bostonscientific.com/}}}\uc2 \f2 ) and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.btgplc.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.btgplc.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ) by no later than 12 noon on the Business Day following the date of this Announcement until the end of the Offer Period: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --      this Announcement; \par    --      the irrevocable undertakings described in paragraphs 5 and 6 above; \par    --      certain financing documents referred to in paragraph 11 above; \par    --      the confidentiality agreement described in paragraph 15 above; and \par    --      the co-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  agreement described in paragraph 15 above. \par    20.          Right to Switch to a Takeover Offer \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bravo Bidco reserves the right, subject to the prior consent of the Panel and to the terms of the Co-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Agreement, to implement the Acquisition by way of a Takeover Offer for the entire issued and to be issued share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2  as an alternative to the Scheme. In such an event, a Takeover Offer will be implemented on the same terms and conditions as those which would apply to the Scheme, subject to appropriate amendments, including, save as otherwise set out in the Co-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Agreement, an Approval Condition set at 90 per cent. in nominal value and of the voting rights attaching to such shares of the shares to which the Takeover Offer relates or such lesser percentage as Bravo Bidco may determine (subject to the consent of the Panel, if necessary), being in any case more than 50 per cent. of the voting rights normally exercisable at a general meeting of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG\f28 \uc2 \f2 , including for this purpose, any such voting rights attaching to BTG Shares that are unconditionally allotted or issued before the Takeover Offer becomes or is declared unconditional as to acceptances, whether pursuant to the exercise of any outstanding subscription or conversion rights or otherwise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If the Acquisition is effected by way of a Takeover Offer, there can be no certainty as to the level of the Approval Condition, or of Bravo Bidco's willingness to waive or lower such Approval Condition. If such Takeover Offer becomes or is declared unconditional in all respects, where:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- acceptances are received from BTG Shareholders such that, together with any other BTG Shares unconditionally acquired, owned or controlled by Bravo Bidco and/or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Scientific\f28 \uc2 \f2  will hold at least 75 per cent. of the voting rights attaching to the BTG Shares, Bravo Bidco intends to request that the then appointed BTG Board (subject to its fiduciary duties) will apply to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the UK Listing Authority respectively to cancel trading in BTG Shares on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 's main market for listed securities and cancel the listing of the BTG Shares on the Daily Official List, which cancellations would eliminate the liquidity of BTG Shares for any remaining BTG Shareholders; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Bravo Bidco receives acceptances under the Takeover Offer in respect of, or otherwise acquires, 90 per cent. or more of the BTG Shares to which the Takeover Offer relates by nominal value and voting rights attaching to such shares, Bravo Bidco intends to exercise its rights pursuant to sections 974 to 991 of the Companies Act to acquire compulsorily the remaining BTG Shares in respect of which the Takeover Offer has not been accepted on the same terms as the Takeover Offer. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    21.          General \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This Announcement does not constitute an offer or an invitation to purchase or subscribe for any securities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In deciding whether or not to vote or procure votes in favour of the resolutions relating to the Scheme at the BTG Meetings in respect of their BTG Shares, BTG Shareholders should rely on the information contained, and follow the procedures described, in the Scheme Document.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Scheme will be subject to the Conditions and certain further terms set out in Appendix I to this Announcement and to the full terms and conditions to be set out in the Scheme Document. Appendix II to this Announcement contains the sources and bases of certain information contained in this Announcement. Appendix III to this Announcement contains a summary of the irrevocable undertakings received in relation to the Acquisition. Appendix IV to this Announcement contains the definitions of certain expressions used in this Announcement. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    22.          Consents \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  has given and has not withdrawn its written consent to the issue of this Announcement with the inclusion therein of the references to its name in the 