\par\par \b \uc2 Denmark's  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves rise;  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened \highlight\uc2  before UK referendum\b0\par\par\uc2 150 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2016\par 16:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 COPENHAGEN, July 4 (Reuters) - Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to 452.3 billion Danish crowns ($67.7 billion) in June from 426.9 billion crowns at the end of May.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by selling 25.2 billion crowns in June to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable against the euro, it said.\par \par \uc2 "The majority of the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place prior to the \b \highlight22\uc2 United Kingdom\b0 \highlight\uc2 's referendum on 23 June on \uc2 European Union\uc2  membership," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The Danish crown briefly strengthened to its strongest level against the euro since 2003 when investors on June 24 flocked to safe-haven assets in the wake of Britain's vote to leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 6.6834 Danish crowns) (Reporting by \uc2 Ole Mikkelsen\uc2 , editing by Larry King) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-7-4T15:10:34.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160704ec7400at0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
