\par\par \b \uc2 Record PLC\uc2  Final Results\b0\par\par\uc2 26,258 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2013\par 08:00\par \uc2 Regulatory News Service\par \uc2 RNS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013   \par \par \uc2 TIDMREC\par \par \uc2 RNS Number : 7191G\par \par \uc2 Record PLC\par \par \uc2 11 June 2013\par \par \uc2 PRESS RELEASE\par \par \uc2 Record plc\par \par \uc2 11 June 2013\par \par \uc2 FINAL RESULTS ANNOUNCEMENT FOR THE YEAR ENDED 31 MARCH 2013\par \par \uc2 Record plc\uc2 , the specialist \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager, today announces its audited results for the year ended 31 March 2013.\par \par \uc2 Financial headlines:\par \par \uc2 -- AUME(1) $34.8bn at 31 March 2013 (up 13%)\par \par \uc2 -- AUME GBP22.9bn at 31 March 2013 (up 19%)\par \par \uc2 -- Revenue of GBP18.6m (down 9%)\par \par \uc2 -- Pre-tax profit of GBP6.1m (down 9%)\par \par \uc2 -- Operating profit margin to 31 March 2013 of 32% unchanged on prior year.\par \par \uc2 -- Financial position remains strong with net assets of GBP32.3m at 31 March 2013 (2012: GBP28.6m); net cash of GBP29.0m (2012: GBP24.6m)\par \par \uc2 -- Basic EPS of 1.98p per share (2012: 2.23p)\par \par \uc2 -- Proposed final dividend for the year to 31 March 2013 is 1.50p per share giving a total dividend in respect of the period of 1.50p per share (2012: 1.50p).\par \par \uc2 Key developments:\par \par \uc2 -- Client numbers increased to 44 by 31 March 2013 (2012: 41)\par \par \uc2 -- Product mix stable through year\par \par \uc2 -- First live multi-strategy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  mandate started during the year\par \par \uc2 -- Positive investment performance in the year from active FRB(2) ,FRB index and Emerging Market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategies\par \par \uc2 (1)As a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager Record manages only the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and not the underlying assets, therefore its "assets under management" are notional rather than tangible. To distinguish this from the AUM of conventional asset managers, Record uses the concept of Assets under Management Equivalents ("AUME") and by convention this is quoted in US dollars.\par \par \uc2 (2)FRB =Forward Rate Bias is the observed tendency of higher interest rate \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' total return to outperform that of lower interest rate \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Commenting on the results, Neil Record, Chairman of Record plc, said:\par \par \uc2 "The year to 31 March 2013 saw encouraging growth in both AUME and client numbers, as well as stabilisation of the product mix and operating margin. The decline in revenue to GBP18.6m, whilst mitigated to some extent by a cost reduction programme, largely reflects the full-year effect of changes in product mix experienced in prior years.\par \par \uc2 "Developments in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets (such as the weakness of the Japanese Yen in response to aggressive policy measures) created opportunities for our return-seeking products during the year and the tentative re-emergence of trending in certain \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs also benefited many of our strategies.\par \par \uc2 "We have developed our suite of \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for Return products further through the year with the start of our first multi-strategy mandate incorporating the first live \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  value programmes, and our emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy live track record passed the three year landmark, an important step in gaining acceptance in the institutional market place.\par \par \uc2 "Growth in AUME and client numbers, and stabilisation of product mix and margin, have established a firm foundation from which to grow further. It is therefore encouraging that since the start of the current financial year, we have commenced a combined passive and dynamic hedging programme with AUME of approximately $1.7 billion, and more recently have been selected (subject to contract) for a significant passive hedging mandate."\par \par \uc2 Analyst briefing\par \par \uc2 There will be a presentation for analysts at 9.30am on Tuesday 11 June 2013 in the Copperfield Room, Holborn Bars, 138-142 Holborn, London, EC1N 2NQ. A copy of the presentation will be made available on the Group's website at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.recordcm.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.recordcm.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For further information, please contact:\par \par \uc2 Record plc\uc2 : +44 1753 852222\par \par \uc2 Neil Record - Chairman\par \par \uc2 James Wood-Collins\uc2  - Chief Executive Officer\par \par \uc2 Steve Cullen - Chief Financial Officer\par \par \uc2 MHP Communications +44 20 3128 8100\par \par \uc2 Nick Denton, John Olsen, Vicky Watkins\par \par \uc2 Consolidated statement of comprehensive income\par \par \uc2 Year ended 31 March\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                                    2013       2012 \par                                                 GBP'000    GBP'000 \par --------------------------------------------  ---------  --------- \par  Revenue                                         18,552     20,535 \par  Cost of sales                                    (221)      (252) \par --------------------------------------------  ---------  --------- \par  Gross profit                                    18,331     20,283 \par  Administrative expenses                       (12,343)   (13,430) \par  Loss on financial instruments held \par   as part of disposal group                        (68)      (299) \par --------------------------------------------  ---------  --------- \par  Operating profit        