 losses are recognised through profit or loss.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 From time to time, the Group injects capital into funds operated by the Group to trial new products (seed capital). If the Group is able to exercise control over such a seeded fund by holding a majority interest (whether the majority interest is held by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Record plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  alone, or by combining the interests of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Record plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  and its Directors), then such funds are considered to be under control of the Group and as such the fund becomes a subsidiary of the Group in accordance with SIC-12 and IAS 27.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group consolidates the assets of its subsidiaries on a line by line basis, but where the Group is actively seeking to reduce its holding in the fore-mentioned seeded funds within twelve months through the sale of further units in these funds to external investors, and the subsequent redemption of Record's own investment, the investments in the funds are classified as being a disposal group held for sale as it is considered highly probable that the funds will not remain under the control of the Group one year after the original investment was made. [ 11-06-13 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If the Group still retains control of the funds after this time, the Group considers whether an extension of the one year period is applicable. If no extension to the period is applicable, then the funds will cease to be classified as held for sale and will be consolidated in full.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In December 2010, the Group invested GBP1,000,000 in the Record \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FTSE FRB10 Index Fund and a further GBP1,000,000 in the Record \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Emerging Market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Fund, and these were accounted for as a disposal group held for sale on the basis described above. In both cases, the Group still retained control over each of the funds twelve months after the original investment. Consequently, from 31 December 2011, both funds ceased to be classified as held for sale and are now consolidated in full, on a line by line basis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In May 2011, the Group invested GBP1,000,000 in the Record \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - Euro Stress Fund, the only other investor in the fund was Neil Record, a Director of Record plc. The Group retained control over this fund from its inception, through to its liquidation in September 2012. The investment in the fund was classified as being a disposal group held for sale.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                      Group               Company \par ----------------------------  -------------------  ------------------ \par                                    2013      2012      2013      2012 \par                                 GBP'000   GBP'000   GBP'000   GBP'000 \par ----------------------------  ---------  --------  --------  -------- \par  Seed capital classified \par   as being a disposal group \par   held for sale                       -     1,075         -       911 \par ----------------------------  ---------  --------  --------  -------- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The underlying assets of the funds are cash deposits and forward exchange contracts with tenors of three months or less which are accounted for as derivatives measured at fair value through profit or loss under IAS 39.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The net loss on financial instruments held as part of a disposal group is as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                     Group              Company \par ---------------------------  ------------------  ------------------ \par                                  2013      2012      2013      2012 \par                               GBP'000   GBP'000   GBP'000   GBP'000 \par -----------------