ord plc and four external investors have purchased units in the two funds currently seeded by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Record plc\f28 \uc2 \f2 , i.e. the Record \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - FTSE FRB10 Index Fund, the Record \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - Emerging Market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Fund, and previously, also the Record \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - Euro Stress Fund. The mark to market value of these units represents the only non-controlling interests in the Group.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The two existing funds are considered to be under control of the Group through majority interests. The Record \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - Euro Stress Fund was considered to be under control of the Group throughout its existence.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mark to market value of external holding in seeded funds consolidated into the accounts of the Record Group\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                           2013      2012 \par                                        GBP'000   GBP'000 \par ------------------------------------  --------  -------- \par  Record \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - FTSE FRB10 Index \par   Fund                                     871       528 \par  Record \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - Emerging Market \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Fund                          2,775     1,572 \par  Record \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - Euro Stress Fund          -       163 \par  Total                                   3,646     2,263 \par ------------------------------------  --------  -------- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 23. Financial risk management\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group's current activities result in the following financial risks and management responses to those risks in order to minimise any resulting adverse effects on the Group's financial performance.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Objectives, policies and processes for managing risk and the methods used to measure the risk\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial assets principally comprise trade receivables, cash and cash equivalents and derivative financial assets. Financial liabilities comprise trade and other payables and derivative financial liabilities. The main risks arising from financial instruments are credit risk, liquidity risk, foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk and interest rate risk each of which is discussed in further detail below.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group monitors and mitigates financial risk on a consolidated basis. The Group has implemented a framework to manage the risks of its business and to ensure that the Directors have in place risk management practices appropriate to a listed company. The management of risk is directed by the Board and reviewed by the Audit and Risk Committee.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company's material financial instruments are investments in the seeded funds, and balances due to/from Group undertakings. The Company's financial risk is managed as part of the Group financial risk management process and therefore separate disclosures for the Company have not been provided.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Credit risk\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Record plc\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Risk Management Committee has established a credit risk policy to ensure that it only trades with counterparties that meet requirements consistent with the Group's agreed risk appetite. The Chief Financial Officer is responsible for reviewing the Group's credit exposure and ensuring that any credit concerns are raised to the Risk Management Committee and that action is taken to mitigate these risks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group invests some of its surplus funds in high quality liquid market instruments. Such investments have a maturity no greater than three months. To reduce the risk of counterparty default the Group deposits the rest of its surplus funds in approved high quality banks; the financial institutions involved have high credit ratings assigned by international credit agencies. The Group operates a policy of restricting its exposure to any single bank to a maximum of GBP10m. All banking counterparties used to hold Group cash have a credit rating EQUIVALENT TO a3 (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) or better.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group's maximum exposure to credit risk is as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                                 2013      2012 \par  Financial assets at 31 March                GBP'000   GBP'000 \par ------------------------------------------  --------  -------- \par  Trade receivables                             4,825     4,268 \par  Other receivables                                40       216 \par  Held for sale financial assets (disposal \par   group)                                           -     1,075 \par  Other financial assets at fair value \par   through profit or loss                          43        33 \par  Cash and cash equivalents                    29,025    24,572 \par ------------------------------------------  --------  -------- \par                                               33,933    30,164 \par ------------------------------------------  --------  -------- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The debtors' age analysis is also evaluated on a regular basis for potential doubtful debts. It is management's opinion that no provision for doubtful debts is required. The table below is an analysis of financial assets by due date:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Carrying     Neither   0-3 months   More than \par                         amount    impaired     past due    3 months \par                                   nor 