\par\par \b \uc2 Teledyne Tech Inc Offer for \uc2 Intelek plc\b0\par\par\uc2 15,940 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 2010\par 08:00\par \uc2 Regulatory News Service\par \uc2 RNS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par \par TIDMITK \par  \par RNS Number : 6942N \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Teledyne Technologies Incorporated\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par 16 June 2010 \par  \par ? \par NOT FOR RELEASE, PUBLICATION OR DISTRIBUTION, IN WHOLE OR IN PART, DIRECTLY OR \par INDIRECTLY, IN, INTO OR FROM ANY JURISDICTION WHERE TO DO SO WOULD CONSTITUTE A \par VIOLATION OF THE RELEVANT LAWS OR REGULATIONS OF SUCH JURISDICTION \par 16 June 2010 \par FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE \par                             RECOMMENDED CASH OFFER \par  \par                                       BY \par  \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 TELEDYNE TECHNOLOGIES\f28 \uc2 \f2  INCORPORATED \par  \par                                       FOR \par  \par  INTELEK PLC \par  \par SUMMARY \par * The Boards of Teledyne and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  are pleased to announce that they have \par reached agreement on the terms of a recommended cash offer to be made by \par Teledyne for the entire issued and to be issued ordinary share capital of \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . It is intended that the Offer will be implemented by way of a public \par offer under the Code. \par * Under the terms of the Offer, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders will receive 32 pence in \par cash for each \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share (the "Offer Price"), valuing the entire existing \par issued ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  at approximately GBP28 million. \par * The Offer Price of 32 pence per \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share represents a premium of \par approximately: \par -106.5 per cent. to the Closing Price of 15.50 pence on 15 June 2010, being the \par last Business Day prior to the date of this announcement; and \par -117 per cent. to the average Closing Price of 14.75 pence for the twelve months \par prior to and ending on 15 June 2010, being the last Business Day prior to the \par date of this announcement. \par * Teledyne is a NYSE listed company with a market capitalisation of \par approximately US$1.4 billion. With 2009 revenues of approximately US$1.8 \par billion, Teledyne is a leading provider of sophisticated electronic components \par and subsystems, instrumentation and communications products and the acquisition \par of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  offers Teledyne the opportunity to extend its presence and know-how \par in activities adjacent to its current ones. \par * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  is an AIM quoted company which designs and manufactures electronic \par systems for satellite and microwave communication with a focus on the defence \par and satellite communications markets. \par * The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, who have been so advised by Altium, consider the terms \par of the Offer to be fair and reasonable so far as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders are \par concerned. In providing their advice, Altium has taken into account the \par commercial assessments of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors. Accordingly, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Directors intend unanimously to recommend that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders accept the \par Offer, as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors have irrevocably undertaken to do in respect of \par their beneficial shareholdings which amount, in aggregate, to 4,906,523 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Shares, representing approximately 5.62 per cent of the existing ordinary share \par capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . These undertakings will remain binding in the event of a \par competing offer being made for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  and will cease to be binding only if the \par Offer lapses or is withdrawn. \par * Teledyne has also received an irrevocable undertaking from Rights & Issues \par Investment Trust PLC to accept the Offer in respect of its 12,500,000 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Shares, representing approximately 14.31 per cent of the existing issued share \par capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . This undertaking ceases to be binding in the event that, \par before this shareholder has accepted the Offer, a Competing Offer is made for \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  where the value of such offer is not less than 35.5 pence per \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Share, or if the Offer lapses or is withdrawn. \par * Accordingly, in aggregate, and including the shareholdings of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Directors, Teledyne has received Irrevocable Undertakings to accept the Offer in \par respect of 17,406,523 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares, representing approximately 19.92 per cent. \par of the existing issued ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par * In addition, Teledyne has received a best endeavours undertaking from \par Discretionary Unit Fund Managers Limited to ensure that Discretionary Unit Fund \par and its Trustee, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC plc\f28 \uc2 \f2 , accept the Offer in respect of the 5,000,000 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Shares held by them, representing approximately 5.72 per cent of the existing \par issued share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . This undertaking ceases to be binding in the \par event that, before this shareholder has accepted the Offer, a competing offer is \par made for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  where the value of such offer is not less than 35.5 pence per \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share, or if the Offer lapses or is withdrawn. \par * The aggregate of all these undertakings in respect of 22,406,523 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Shares, represent approximately 25.64 per cent of the ordinary share capital of \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par Commenting on the Offer, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Robert Mehrabian\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Chairman, President and Chief \par Executive Officer of Teledyne, said: \par "We are delighted that the directors of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  have decided unanimously to \par recommend the Offer to their shareholders which is at a significant premium to \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's share price in the 12 months prior to the Offer date. The combination \par of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  with Teledyne should place \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a much stronger position to \par realise its growth potential". \par Commenting on the Offer, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ian Brodie\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Chief Executive Officer of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said: \par "The directors of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  have focused our strategy on further developing our \par satellite and microwave communications business as a core value driver for the \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 . This Offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  is at a substantial premium and we \par unanimously recommend that shareholders accept this Offer". \par This summary should be read in conjunction with the full text of this \par announcement including the Appendices to this announcement. In particular, the \par Offer will be subject to the conditions set out in Appendix I to this \par announcement and to the further terms that will be set out in the Offer \par Documentation. \par -  Appendix I sets out the Conditions and further terms to implementation of the \par Offer. \par  \par -  Appendix II sets out the sources and bases of certain financial information \par contained in this announcement. \par  \par -  Appendix III contains details of the Irrevocable Undertakings and best \par endeavours undertaking referred to in this announcement. \par  \par -  Appendix IV contains the definitions o