ng \par statements are not guarantees of future performance or results and involve risks \par and uncertainties because they relate to events and depend on circumstances that \par will occur in the future. Actual results may differ materially. \par There are a number of factors that could cause actual results and developments \par to differ materially from those expressed or implied by such forward-looking \par statements. These factors include, but are not limited to, unanticipated issues \par associated with the satisfaction of the Conditions; issues associated with \par obtaining necessary regulatory approvals and the terms and conditions of such \par approvals; the inability to integrate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  successfully within Teledyne or to \par realise synergies from such integration within the time periods anticipated; and \par changes in anticipated costs related to the acquisition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Additional \par factors that could cause actual results and developments to differ materially \par include, among other things: \par -     unanticipated changes in revenue, margins, costs, and capital \par expenditures; \par -     issues associated with new product introductions; \par -     foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fluctuations; \par -     increased raw material prices; \par -     unexpected issues associated with the availability of local suppliers and \par skilled labour; \par -     the risks associated with growth; \par -     geographic factors and political and economic risks; \par -     actions of competitors; \par -     changes in economic or industry conditions generally or in the markets \par served by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Teledyne; \par -     the state of financial and credit markets; \par -     efficiencies and capacity utilisation of facilities; \par -     issues related to new facilities and expansion of existing facilities; \par -     work stoppages, labour negotiations, and labour rates; \par -     government approval and funding of projects; \par -     the ability of Teledyne's and/or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's customers to receive financing; \par -     the ability to complete and appropriately integrate restructurings, \par consolidations, acquisitions, divestitures, strategic alliances, and joint \par ventures; and \par -     risk and other factors cited in Teledyne's filings with the SEC. \par Neither Teledyne nor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  undertakes any obligation to update or revise \par forward-looking statements, whether as a result of new information, future \par events or otherwise. Forward-looking statements only speak as of the date on \par which they are made. \par Publication on websites \par A copy of this announcement is and will be available free of charge, subject to \par certain restrictions relating to persons resident in Restricted Jurisdictions, \par for inspection on Teledyne's website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.teledyne.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.teledyne.com}}}\uc2 \f2  and on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.intelek.plc.uk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.intelek.plc.uk}}}\uc2 \f2  during the course of the Offer. \par  \par Rule 2.10 Disclosure \par In accordance with Rule 2.10 of the Code, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  confirms that on 15 June 2010 \par it had 87,376,072 ordinary shares in issue all with equal voting rights. The \par International Securities Identification Number for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  ordinary shares \par is GB0000084805. \par  \par  \par 16 June 2010 \par  \par NOT FOR RELEASE, PUBLICATION OR DISTRIBUTION, IN WHOLE OR IN PART, DIRECTLY OR \par INDIRECTLY, IN, INTO OR FROM ANY JURISDICTION WHERE TO DO SO WOULD CONSTITUTE A \par VIOLATION OF THE RELEVANT LAWS OR REGULATIONS OF SUCH JURISDICTION. \par  \par                             RECOMMENDED CASH OFFER \par  \par                                       BY \par  \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 TELEDYNE TECHNOLOGIES\f28 \uc2 \f2  INCORPORATED \par  \par                                       FOR \par  \par  INTELEK PLC \par  \par  \par  \par  \par 1. INTRODUCTION \par  \par The Boards of Teledyne and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  are pleased to announce that agreement has \par been reached on the terms of a recommended cash offer to be made by Teledyne for \par the entire issued and to be issued ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par  \par 2. THE OFFER \par  \par The Offer, which will be subject to the Conditions and further terms set out \par below and in Appendix I, and to be set out in the Offer Documentation when \par issued, is being made on the following basis: \par  \par          32 pence in cash                       for each \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share. \par  \par The Offer values \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's existing issued ordinary share capital at \par approximately GBP28 million. \par  \par The Offer will be made cum-dividend in respect of the Final Dividend. The Offer \par Price has been determined on the basis that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders will \par neither be paid nor will they be entitled to retain the Final Dividend of 0.30 \par pence per \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share. Accordingly, the consideration of 32 pence per \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Share paid to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders pursuant to the Offer will be reduced by the \par amount of the Final Dividend, to the extent that such Final Dividend is paid to \par any \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders. \par  \par The Offer Price represents a premium of approximately: \par  \par -    106.5 per cent. to the Closing Price of 15.50 pence per \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share on 15 \par June 2010, being the last Business Day prior to the date of this announcement; \par and \par -    117 per cent. to the average Closing Price of 14.75 pence for the twelve \par months prior to and ending on 15 June 2010, being the last Business Day prior to \par the date of this announcement. \par The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares will be acquired by Teledyne fully paid and free from all \par liens, equitable interests, charges, encumbrances, rights of pre-emption and any \par other third party rights or interests whatsoever and together with all rights \par existing as at 8 June 2010 or thereafter attaching thereto, including, without \par limitation, the right to receive and retain, in full, all dividends (including \par the Final Dividend) and other distributions (if any) declared, made or paid or \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 16-06-10 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par any other return of capital (whether by way of reduction of share capital or \par share premium account or otherwise) made on or after 8 June 2010 in respect of \par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares.  If any dividend or other distribution in respect of the \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares is declared, paid or made on or after 8 June 2010, Teledyne \par reserves the right to reduce the consideration payable for each \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share \par under the terms of the Offer by the amount per \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share of such dividend or \par distribution. \par  \par 3. IRREVOCABLE UNDERTAKINGS AND BEST ENDEAVOURS UNDERTAKING \par  \par Teledyne has received Irrevocable Undertakings to accept the Offer from the \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors in respect of, in aggregate, 4,906,523 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares \par representing approximately 5.62 per cent. of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's issued ordinary share \par capital.  These undertakings will remain binding in the event of a competing \par offer being made for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  and will cease to be binding only if the Offer \par lapses or is withdrawn. \par  \par Teledyne has also received an Irrevocable Undertaking from Rights & Issues \par Investment Trust PLC to accept the Offer in respect of its 12,500,000 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Shares, representing approximately 14.31 per cent of the existing issued share \par capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . This undertaking ceases to be binding in the event that, \par before this shareholder has accepted the Offer, a Competing Offer is made for \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  where the value of such offer is not less than 35.5 pence per \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Share, or if the Offer lapses or is withdrawn. \par  \par Accordingly, in aggregate, and including the shareholdings of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Directors, Teledyne has received Irrevocable Undertakings to accept the Offer in \par respect of 17,406,523 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares, representing approximately 19.92 per cent. \par of the existing issued ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par  \par In addition, Teledyne has received a best endeavours undertaking from \par Discretionary Unit Fund Managers Limited to ensure that Discretionary Unit Fund \par and its Trustee, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC plc\f28 \uc2 \f2 , accept the Offer in respect of the 5,000,000 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Shares held by them, representing approximately 5.72 per cent of the existing \par issued share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . This undertaking ceases to be binding in the \par event that, before this shareholder has accepted the Offer, a competing offer is \par made for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  where the value of such offer is not less than 35.5 pence per \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share, or if the Offer lapses or is withdrawn. \par  \par The aggregate of all these undertakings in respect of 22,406,523 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares, \par represent approximately 25.64 per cent of the ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par  \par Further details of these Irrevocable Undertakings and best endeavours \par undertaking to accept the Offer are set out in Appendix III to this \par announcement. \par  \par  \par 4. INFORMATION RELATING TO TELEDYNE \par  \par Teledyne is a leading provider of sophisticated electronic components and \par subsystems, instrumentation and communications products, including defence \par electronics, monitoring and control instrumentation for marine, environmental \par and industrial applications, harsh environment interconnect products, data \par acquisition and communications equipment for air transport and business \par aircraft, and components and subsystems for wireless and satellite \par communications. \par  \par Teledyne is organised by market in four business segments: \par  \par (i)     Electronics and Communications (defence electronics, including microwave \par devices, interconnects and imaging sensors; electronic instrumentation; and \par other commercial electronics, including aircraft information management \par systems); \par (ii)    Engineered Systems (engineered systems for defence, space, environmental \par and nuclear applications); \par (iii)   Aerospace Engines and Components (OEM and aftermarket general aviation \par piston engines and spare parts); and \par (iv)   Energy and Power Systems (energy generation systems, aviation batteries \par and military turbine engines). \par  \par Teledyne employs approximately 8,000 people around the world and is listed on \par the New York Stock Exchange (ticker: TDY), with a market capitalisation of \par approximately US$1.4 billion. \par  \par Teledyne has a large established United Kingdom presence, with over 400 \par employees. In 2008, Teledyne further expanded its United Kingdom presence with \par the acquisitions of TSS (International) Limited, Filtronic Defence Limited and \par Cormon Limited. Sales from United Kingdom \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  currently represent \par approximately US$90 million. \par  \par For the fiscal years ended 3 January 2010 and 28 December 2008, Teledyne \par reported (all on a consolidated basis) revenues of US$1,765 million and US$1,893 \par million respectively, and net attributable earnings of US$113 million and US$111 \par million respectively. As at 3 January 2010, Teledyne reported net assets of \par US$667 million. \par  \par 5. INFORMATION RELATING TO INTELEK \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  is a group of companies which designs and manufactures electronic \par systems for satellite and microwave communication and is a specialist \par manufacturer for the aerospace market. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  is a leading supplier in the \par global communications market. \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's strategy focuses on the application of specialist skills to selected \par market niches. These skills include microwave frequency design, digital signal \par processing, thermal modelling and microwave circuit processing and sub assembly. \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  has three divisions as detailed below: \par  \par (i) \f28 \uc2 \f2 Paradise Datacom\f28 \uc2 \f2 Paradise Datacom\f28 \uc2 \f2  designs and manufactures satellite modems, transceivers, block \par up-converters, solid state power amplifiers, low noise amplifiers and associated \par equipment for the terrestrial segment of the satellite communications market. \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Paradise Datacom\f28 \uc2 \f2  has sales, design and manufacturing facilities in both the \par United Kingdom and the United States. \par  \par (ii) Labtech \par Labtech is a manufacturer of microwave circuit solutions with specialist \par capabilities in design, manufacturing, assembly and testing across many \par technologies, product and market applications from defence electronics, global \par telecommunications to space and satellite communications. Labtech is based in \par the United Kingdom. \par  \par (iii) CML \par CML manufactures precision machined and composite aerostructures for military \par and commercial aircraft. CML is based in the United Kingdom. \par  \par Since the year ended 31 March 2010, both \f28 \uc2 \f2 Paradise Datacom\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Labtech have \par traded at similar levels to the previous year. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Paradise Datacom\f28 \uc2 \f2 's strength of \par product range and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's success in penetrating new government programmes, \par combined with exciting long-term growth sectors such as internet and HDTV, give \par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Board confidence for the future. Labtech is expecting a similar \par pattern to last year, with a much stronger second half. CML has good sales \par expectations for the current year but its results are likely to be affected by \par the GBP0.4 million step function increase in composites' costs from the new \par enhanced facility, an important investment in the future of this \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par  \par For the year ended 31 March 2010 total group revenues were GBP37.7 million and \par reported operating profit was GBP3.9 million. \par  \par  \par 6. BACKGROUND TO AND REASONS FOR THE OFFER \par  \par Teledyne sees clear strategic benefits from a combination of the two businesses. \par Teledyne believes that Teledyne and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  share the same overall strategy - a \par focus on high reliability products for particular market segments. The \par acquisition by Teledyne of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  will allow the Teledyne Group and \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  to extend their presence and know-how in activities adjacent to \par their current ones. Teledyne believes that the products of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Paradise \par Datacom\f28 \uc2 \f2  division are complementary to, and do not overlap with, Teledyne's own \par microwave products.  In particular, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Paradise Datacom\f28 \uc2 \f2 's high power solid state \par amplifiers and modems for commercial customers complement Teledyne's strong \par position in broadband, high power TWT and lower power solid state subsystems for \par military customers.  Teledyne believes it can provide expanded access to \par military customers for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Paradise Datacom\f28 \uc2 \f2 's products and technology. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \par Labtech subsidiary fits well with Teledyne's microwave communication businesses \par and can provide Teledyne with access to non-United States defence contractors. \par By combining Teledyne's and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's capabilities, Teledyne believes that the \par enlarged group will be able to offer, over time, an enhanced range of complete \par high-power TWT and GaAs and GaN-based high power solid-state amplifier systems \par for communications, radar and electronic warfare applications. Finally, Teledyne \par believes that its capabilities in sourcing and manufacturing should enhance \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's overall competitiveness and result in improved growth prospects for \par the enlarged group. \par  \par 7. THE RECOMMENDATION \par  \par The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, who have been so advised by Altium, consider the terms of \par the Offer to be fair and reasonable so far as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders are \par concerned. In providing their advice to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, Altium has taken \par into account the commercial assessments of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors. \par  \par Accordingly, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors intend unanimously to recommend that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Shareholders accept the Offer, as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors have irrevocably \par undertaken to do in respect of their beneficial shareholdings which amount, in \par aggregate, to 4,906,523 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares, representing approximately 5.62 per cent \par of the existing ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par  \par 8. BACKGROUND TO AND REASONS FOR THE RECOMMENDATION \par  \par The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Board has over a period of time moved the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's strategic \par focus towards its current core activities of satellite communications and \par microwave components, which it was believed would deliver best value to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Shareholders. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Board believes that the value of the Offer validates \par this strategy. \par  \par The terms of the Offer from Teledyne represent a significant premium to the \par Closing Price on 15 June 2010 (being the last Business Day prior to the date of \par this announcement) and provide certainty for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders through \par the ability to realise their investment in cash at a level that has not been \par available on the market in the last 5 years. In addition, Teledyne has indicated \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 16-06-10 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that under its ownership Teledyne will continue to develop and support the \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  businesses and further develop its market position, in line with its \par stated strategy. \par  \par 9. TELEDYNE'S INTENTIONS FOR INTELEK AND INTELEK'S MANAGEMENT AND EMPLOYEES \par  \par Teledyne intends to continue the businesses of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 , including supporting \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's current activities. Following completion of the acquisition, Teledyne \par will consider strategic alternatives for CML, which may after review include a \par disposal of the business. Teledyne also intends to transfer the ownership of \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's United States subsidiaries so that they are directly owned by Teledyne \par or a US subsidiary of Teledyne. Teledyne has confirmed to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Board that \par there are currently no other planned major restructurings or changes in location \par of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and places of business; however, in time Teledyne may \par close \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's head office and transfer the responsibilities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \par corporate management team to other locations. \par  \par The Board of Teledyne has given assurances to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors that, \par following the Offer becoming Effective, the existing employment rights of all \par employees of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  will be fully safeguarded. Teledyne's current plans do not \par involve any material change in the conditions of employment of the employees of \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . In addition, Teledyne has agreed that, upon completion of the Offer, \par the existing pension rights of all the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  employees will be observed at \par least to the extent required by the applicable law.  The Teledyne Directors \par believe that following completion of the Offer, the financial covenant of \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  will be significantly improved, providing additional comfort to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par pension scheme members. \par  \par Except as set out below, upon the Offer becoming Effective, each of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Directors will resign from the Boards of each company within the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par Teledyne anticipates that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ian Brodie\f28 \uc2 \f2  will cease to be the Chief Executive of \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  following the Offer becoming Effective. \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 John Restivo\f28 \uc2 \f2  will continue in his position as the President of the United States \par and United Kingdom \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Paradise Datacom\f28 \uc2 \f2 . It is intended that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kevin \par Edwards\f28 \uc2 \f2  will cease to be the Finance Director of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  following the Offer \par becoming Effective, however, he may continue as an employee or a consultant for \par a transitional period to be agreed with Teledyne. No incentivisation \par arrangements have been proposed to any member of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  management who is \par interested in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares. \par  \par  \par 10. INTELEK SHARE SCHEMES \par  \par The Offer will extend to any \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares unconditionally allotted or issued \par and fully paid on or prior to the date on which the Offer closes (or, such \par earlier date as Teledyne may, subject to the Code, decide) pursuant to the \par exercise of options under the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share Schemes or as a result of the \par vesting of awards pursuant to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share Schemes. \par  \par To the extent that such options or awards have not been exercised or vested, \par participants in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share Schemes will be written to separately and \par appropriate proposals will be made to such participants in due course.  It is \par currently intended that such proposals will be made once the Offer becomes or is \par declared unconditional in all respects. \par  \par 11. INDUCEMENT FEE AND OTHER ARRANGEMENTS \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Teledyne have entered into an agreement under which \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  has \par agreed to pay Teledyne an amount equal to one per cent of the value of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par calculated by reference to the Offer Price and the fully diluted ordinary share \par capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  in accordance with Rule 21.2 of the Code (inclusive, in \par certain circumstances, of VAT if applicable) in the event that: \par  \par \u183\'00\'B7     following the date of this announcement, a Competing Offer is announced \par and the Offer is not made or is made but fails to become unconditional in all \par respects and lapses or is withdrawn; or \par  \par \u183\'00\'B7     in or following this announcement, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors do not \par respectively make or reconfirm a unanimous and unqualified recommendation to the \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders in the Offer Document or Scheme document (as the case may \par be) to accept the Offer, or vote in favour of the proposed resolution (in the \par case of a Scheme), as the case may be, or all, or a majority of, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Directors withdraw or qualify or adversely modify for whatever reason their \par recommendation of the Offer or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  notifies Teledyne of its decision not to \par proceed with the Offer and/or the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors agree to recommend a \par Competing Offer; or \par  \par \u183\'00\'B7     following the date of this announcement, the Panel allows Teledyne to not \par make or withdraw the Offer by reason of a breach of the conditions to the Offer \par which arises as a result of an act or omission of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  beyond Teledyne's \par control, other than those conditions relating to acceptance; or \par  \par \u183\'00\'B7     following the date of this announcement, the alteration by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  of its \par issued share capital or rights attaching thereto (save in respect of shares \par issued to directors or employees of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  pursuant to the lawful \par exercise of rights currently granted to them under the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share Schemes); \par or \par  \par \u183\'00\'B7     following the date of this announcement, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  breaches any material \par terms of an implementation agreement that the parties entered into prior to the \par making of this announcement in the event that the offer is implemented by way of \par a Scheme. \par  \par Nothing in such agreement obliges \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  to pay any amount which the Panel \par determines would not be permitted by Rule 21.2 of the Code. \par  \par In the above agreement, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  has also agreed not to recommend, declare or \par make any dividend or other distribution following the date of this announcement \par except that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  can pay any dividends declared prior to the date of this \par announcement. \par  \par Teledyne and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  also entered into an agreement pursuant to which Teledyne \par agreed to pay a sum of GBP50,000 (inclusive of VAT) to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  in certain \par circumstances if Teledyne notified \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  prior to the making of this \par announcement that it did not intend to make a formal offer. \par  \par 12. OFFER FINANCING AND CASH CONFIRMATION \par  \par The total cash consideration payable pursuant to the Offer is estimated to be \par GBP28.2 million. Teledyne intends to finance the Offer from its existing cash \par resources. \par  \par Rothschild, financial adviser to Teledyne, is satisfied that sufficient \par resources are available to satisfy in full the cash consideration payable to \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders pursuant to the terms of the Offer. \par  \par 13. DISCLOSURE OF INTERESTS IN INTELEK SHARES \par  \par Save as disclosed herein, none of Teledyne or any of its directors or, so far as \par Teledyne is aware, any person acting in concert with Teledyne has: (i) any \par interest in, or right to subscribe for, any \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares, nor does any such \par person have any short position (whether conditional or absolute and whether in \par the money or otherwise), including any short position under a derivative, any \par agreement to sell or any delivery obligation or right to require another person \par to purchase or take delivery; or (ii) has borrowed or lent any \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares. \par Furthermore, no arrangement exists with Teledyne, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  or an associate of \par Teledyne or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  in relation to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares. For these purposes, an \par "arrangement" includes any indemnity or option arrangement, any agreement or any \par understanding, formal or informal, of whatever nature, relating to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Shares which may be an inducement to deal or refrain from dealing in such \par securities. \par  \par 14. CONFIRMATION REGARDING OPENING POSITION DISCLOSURE \par  \par Teledyne confirms that it will on the date of this announcement be making an \par Opening Position Disclosure which discloses the details required to be disclosed \par by it under Rule 8.1 (a) of the Code \par  \par 15. COMPULSORY ACQUISITION AND CANCELLATION OF TRADING \par  \par If Teledyne receives acceptances of the Offer in respect of, or otherwise \par acquires, 90 per cent. or more of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares to which the Offer relates \par and assuming all other Conditions of the Offer have been satisfied or waived (if \par they are capable of being waived), Teledyne intends to exercise its rights \par pursuant to the provisions of sections 979 to 991 (inclusive) of the Companies \par Act to acquire compulsorily the remaining \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares to which the Offer \par relates on the same terms as the Offer. \par  \par If the Offer becomes or is declared unconditional in all respects and Teledyne \par receives acceptances of the Offer which result in Teledyne and/or any other \par members of the Teledyne Group holding \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares carrying in aggregate more \par than 75 per cent. of the total number of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares, Teledyne intends to \par procure that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  applies to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares to \par cease to be admitted to trading on AIM.  Such cancellation will significantly \par reduce the liquidity and marketability of any \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares in respect of which \par the Offer has not been accepted. \par  \par Following such cancellation, Teledyne intends to procure that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  is \par re-registered as a private limited company under the relevant provision of the \par Companies Act. \par  \par 16. WITHDRAWAL RIGHTS \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders will have the ability to withdraw their acceptances only in \par limited circumstances to the extent permitted by applicable law and the Code, as \par will be described in more detail in the Offer Documentation. \par  \par 17. CONDITIONALITY OF THE OFFER \par  \par The Offer will be subject to the Conditions and the further terms set out in \par Appendix I and to the terms and conditions to be set out in the Offer \par Documentation when issued. The Offer will be conditional upon, amongst other \par things: \par  \par (a)  Teledyne receiving valid acceptances of the Offer in respect of not less \par than 90 per cent. of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares to which the Offer relates (or such \par lower percentage as Teledyne may decide) provided that such Condition will not \par be satisfied unless Teledyne and/or any other members of the Wider Teledyne \par Group have acquired or agreed to acquire, whether pursuant to the Offer or \par otherwise, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares carrying in aggregate more than 50 per cent. of the \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 16-06-10 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par voting rights then normally exercisable at general meetings of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 ); and \par  \par (b)  in the event that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 United Kingdom\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Secretary of State serves a special \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  notice pursuant to Section 59 of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 United Kingdom\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Enterprise Act \par 2002, the United Kingdom Secretary of State or the United Kingdom Office of Fair \par Trading indicating in terms satisfactory to Teledyne that the United Kingdom \par Secretary of State does not intend to refer the Offer or any matter arising from \par it to the United Kingdom Competition Commission pursuant to Section 62 of the \par United Kingdom Enterprise Act 2002. \par  \par 18. OVERSEAS SHAREHOLDERS \par  \par The availability of the Offer to persons not resident in and citizens of the \par United Kingdom may be affected by the laws of the relevant jurisdictions in \par which they are located or of which they are citizens. Persons who are not \par resident in or citizens of the United Kingdom should inform themselves of and \par observe any applicable legal or regulatory requirements of their jurisdictions. \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders who are in any doubt regarding such matters should consult \par an appropriate independent professional adviser in the relevant jurisdiction \par without delay. \par  \par Further details in relation to Overseas Shareholders will be contained in the \par Offer Documentation. \par  \par 19. GENERAL \par  \par The Offer Documentation will be posted (other than to persons resident in a \par Restricted Jurisdiction) as soon as reasonably practicable after, and in any \par event within 28 days of, the date of this announcement (unless agreed otherwise \par with the Panel). \par  \par The Offer will be governed by English law and will be subject to the \par jurisdiction of the English courts. The Offer will be subject to the applicable \par requirements of the Code. \par  \par The Offer will be subject to the Conditions and further terms set out in \par Appendix I to this announcement and to the terms and conditions that will be set \par out in the Offer Documentation. \par  \par -  Appendix I sets out the Conditions and further terms to implementation of the \par Offer. \par  \par -  Appendix II sets out the sources and bases of certain financial information \par contained in this announcement. \par  \par -  Appendix III contains details of the Irrevocable Undertakings and best \par endeavours undertaking referred to in this announcement. \par  \par -  Appendix IV contains the definitions of certain terms used in this \par announcement. \par  \par This announcement is not intended to and does not constitute or form part of an \par offer to sell or the solicitation of an offer to subscribe for or buy or an \par invitation to purchase or subscribe for any securities or the solicitation of \par any vote or approval in any jurisdiction pursuant to the Offer or otherwise, nor \par shall there be any sale, issuance or transfer of the securities in any \par jurisdiction in contravention of applicable law. Any response in relation to the \par Offer should be made only on the basis of the information in the Offer \par Documentation or any document by which the Offer is made.  The Offer \par Documentation will be prepared and distributed to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders and, for \par information only to persons with information rights. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Teledyne urge \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders to read the Offer Documentation when it becomes available \par because it will contain important information relating to the Offer. \par Rothschild, which is authorised and regulated in the United Kingdom by the \par Financial Services Authority, is acting for Teledyne as financial adviser in \par relation to the Offer and is not acting for or advising any other person and \par accordingly will not be responsible to any person other than Teledyne for \par providing the protections afforded to the clients of Rothschild or for providing \par advice in relation to the contents of this announcement or any offer or \par arrangements referred to herein or in the Offer Documentation. Neither \par Rothschild nor any of its affiliates owes or accepts any duty, liability or \par responsibility whatsoever (whether direct or indirect, whether in contract, in \par tort, under statute or otherwise) to any person who is not a client of \par Rothschild in connection with this announcement, any statement contained herein \par or otherwise. \par Altium, which is authorised and regulated in the United Kingdom by the Financial \par Services Authority, is acting exclusively for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  and no-one else in \par connection with the Offer and will not be responsible to anyone other than \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  for providing the protections afforded to clients of Altium nor for \par providing advice in relation to the Offer or any other matters referred to \par herein. \par Notice to overseas holders of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares \par The availability of the Offer to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders who are not resident in \par and citizens of the United Kingdom may be affected by the