t be and must not be mailed or otherwise forwarded, distributed or sent in, \par into or from any Restricted Jurisdiction or any other jurisdiction where to do \par so would violate the laws in that jurisdiction. \par Dealing Disclosure Requirements \par Under Rule 8.3(a) of the Code, any person who is interested in 1% or more of any \par class of relevant securities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  must make an Opening Position Disclosure \par following the commencement of the offer period. An Opening Position Disclosure \par must contain details of the person's interests and short positions in, and \par rights to subscribe for, any relevant securities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . An Opening Position \par Disclosure by a person to whom Rule 8.3(a) applies must be made by no later than \par 3.30 pm (London time) on the 10th Business Day following the commencement of the \par offer period. Relevant persons who deal in the relevant securities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par prior to the deadline for making an Opening Position Disclosure must instead \par make a Dealing Disclosure. \par Under Rule 8.3(b) of the Code, any person who is, or becomes, interested in 1% \par or more of any class of relevant securities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  must make a Dealing \par Disclosure if the person deals in any relevant securities \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 . A Dealing \par Disclosure must contain details of the dealing concerned and of the person's \par interests and short positions in, and rights to subscribe for, any relevant \par securities of each \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2 , save to the extent that these details have \par previously been disclosed under Rule 8. A Dealing Disclosure by a person to whom \par Rule 8.3(b) applies must be made by no later than 3.30 pm (London time) on the \par Business Day following the date of the relevant dealing. \par If two or more persons act together pursuant to an agreement or under