onditions 1(B) to 1(J). The Offer \par will lapse unless Conditions 1(B) to 1(J) have been satisfied, fulfilled or, if \par capable of waiver, waived by midnight on the 21st day after the later of the \par first closing date of the Offer and the date on which Condition 1 (A) is \par fulfilled (or in each such case such later date as Teledyne may, with the \par consent of the Panel, decide). \par (B)  Teledyne is under no obligation to waive or determine to be, or treat as, \par fulfilled, any of Conditions 1(B) to 1(J) by a date earlier than the date \par specified above for the fulfilment thereof notwithstanding that the other \par Conditions may at such earlier date have been waived or fulfilled and that there \par are at such earlier date no circumstances indicating that any of such Conditions \par may not be capable of fulfilment. \par (C) Unless otherwise agreed with the Panel, the Offer will lapse if, (1) the \par Offer, or any matter arising from it, is referred to the Competition Commission; \par or (2) following a request to the European Commission under Article 22(1) and/or \par Article 22(2) of the Merger Regulation in relation to the Offer or any part of \par it, which request is accepted by the European Commission, the European \par Commission initiates proceedings under Article 6(1)(c) of the Merger Regulation, \par before 1.00 p.m. on the first closing date of the Offer or the date on which the \par Offer becomes or is declared unconditional as to acceptances, whichever is \par later. \par 3.    Certain further terms of the Offer \par (A) If Teledyne is required by the Panel to make an offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares \par under the provisions of Rule 9 of the Code, Teledyne may make such alterations \par to any of the above Conditions as are necessary to comply with the provisions of \par the Rule. \par (B)  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares acquired under the Offer will be acquired fully paid and \par free from all liens, equities, charges, encumbrances, options, rights of \par pre-emption and any other third party rights and interests of any nature and \par together with all rights now or hereafter attaching or accruing to them, \par including voting rights and the right to receive and retain in full all \par dividends (including the Final Dividend) and other distributions (if any) \par declared, made or paid on or after 8 June 2010. Accordingly, insofar as a \par dividend (including the Final Dividend) and/or a distribution and/or a return of \par capital is proposed, declared, made, paid or becomes payable by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  in \par respect of an \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share on or after 8 June 2010 and prior to the Offer \par becoming or being declared unconditional in all respects or lapsing or being \par withdrawn, Teledyne reserves the right to reduce the price payable under the \par Offer in respect of an \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share by the amount of the dividend and/or \par distribution and/or return of capital except insofar as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share is or \par will be transferred pursuant to the Offer on a basis which entitles Teledyne \par alone to receive the dividend and/or distribution and/or return of capital and \par to retain it. To the extent that a reduction in the price payable pursuant to \par the Offer in respect of an \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share is to apply in respect of a dividend \par and/or distribution and/or return of capital but that reduction in price has not \par been effected, the person to whom the Offer Price is paid in respect of that \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share will be obliged to account to Teledyne for the amount of such \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 16-06-10 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dividend or distribution or return of capital. \par (C) Teledyne reserves the right, with the agreement of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Board and the \par Panel (if required), to elect to implement the Offer by way of scheme(s) of \par arrangement pursuant to Part 26 of the Companies Act. In such event, such offer \par will be implemented on the same terms (subject to appropriate amendments as may \par be required by law or regulation), so far as applicable, as those that would \par apply to the Offer. In particular, Condition 1(A) will not apply and the Scheme \par will become effective and binding following: \par (i)                  approval of the Scheme at the court meeting (or any \par adjournment thereof) by a majority of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders present and \par voting either in person or by proxy representing 75 per cent. or more in value \par of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders; \par (ii)                 the resolutions required to approve and implement the \par Scheme being those set out in the notice of general meeting of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Shareholders being passed by the requisite majority at such general meeting; and \par (iii)                the sanction of the Scheme and confirmation of any \par associated reduction of capital by the Court (in each case with or without \par modification, and any such modification to be on terms reasonably acceptable to \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Teledyne) and an office copy of the order of the Court sanctioning \par the Scheme and confirming the cancellation of share capital which forms part of \par it being delivered for registration to the Registrar of Companies and being \par registered by him. \par (D) If the Offer lapses it will cease to be capable of further acceptance. \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intelek\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders who have accepted the Offer and Teledyne shall then cease \par to be bound by acceptances delivered on or before the date on which the Offer \par lapses. \par (E)  The Offer will not be made, directly or indirectly, in or into, by use of \par the